        // 1.0.55.0 - Pre-fetch now gets TagIds. Confirmed from live responses:
        //            get_asset_tags returns NO TagID (only AssetAttributeId); search_tags
        //            is the only source, and history_get needs one. The matcher was also
        //            reading field names that do not exist ("AttributeName" vs
        //            "AssetAttributeName"), so it returned null every time. Asset hints
        //            are seeded up front so the baseline is narrowed during pre-fetch too
        // 1.0.54.0 - METHOD block now yields to the PRE-FETCHED EVIDENCE status list.
        //            The two were contradicting each other and the model followed METHOD
        // 1.0.53.0 - Pre-fetch now states WHICH steps are already done and why anything is
        //            missing. The model was re-calling get_asset_tags despite the tags
        //            being in front of it, because the METHOD block still told it to
        // 1.0.52.0 - Align the STREAMING path with the verdict path. It had none of the
        //            safeguards: no argument clamps, no zero-id refusal, no budget caps,
        //            no attribute-range narrowing, no usability check, no truncation
        //            repair, no coverage note. Only the OUTPUT differs now
        // 1.0.51.0 - Pre-fetch also runs on the STREAMING path (the popup a user watches),
        //            and no longer calls the verdict-only budget check there, which would
        //            have thrown on a null counter
        // 1.0.50.0 - PRE-FETCH (AnalyzePrefetch, default OFF): gather tag list, baseline
        //            and value series before the model runs, so a verdict takes ONE turn
        //            instead of five. Tools stay available as a fallback; pre-fetched
        //            telemetry satisfies the grounding gate exactly as a tool call does
        // 1.0.49.0 - The FINAL turn is output-bound, not input-bound: measured 1,569
        //            output tokens = 33 s against 10,540 input on the same turn. Cap
        //            viz.series at 24 points (trim, do not reject) and tell the model
        //            that everything it writes after the tools answer delays the result
        // 1.0.48.0 - Accept siteId/assetId in the alert context and present them as
        //            authoritative, so the model skips resolution entirely. The station
        //            is a CODE ("SK") and search_sites matches the NAME ("SAKHUN"), so
        //            resolution could not succeed -- 5 failed lookups in one observed run
        // 1.0.47.0 - Fix CS0103 'sw': the 1.0.45.0 tool_done frame was placed in the
        //            VERDICT branch (stopwatch is swAll there, and that path does not
        //            stream). Moved to the streaming branch where sw is in scope
        // 1.0.46.0 - Evidence limit 200 -> 500. `limit` controls how far FORWARD the
        //            series reaches, not payload size: 200 over a 3-day window ended ~29h
        //            before the incidence, which is the reported gap. 500 + 3-day window
        //            reaches the alert at ~7 KB
        // 1.0.45.0 - SSE "step" frames (model_start / model_done / tool_done) carrying
        //            duration, tokens and result size, so the popup can show a LIVE
        //            progress trail instead of a fixed checklist that hides where the
        //            time goes
        // 1.0.44.0 - History never reached the alert: the API returns the OLDEST rows up
        //            to `limit`, so a 7-day window at ~1 sample/13min covered 4.4 days and
        //            ended 58 h short. Window 7d -> 3d (AnalyzeWindowDays), plus a
        //            coverage note appended to any series that stops before the incidence
        // 1.0.43.0 - SAFETY: refuse tool calls with a zero identifier. get_hist_realtime
        //            with asset_id=0 returned a 3,217-char zero-filled shell that passed
        //            the usability check and, being history-class, would have grounded a
        //            verdict on no telemetry
        // 1.0.42.0 - The evidence chain needs NO SiteId: history_get / get_asset_tags /
        //            get_tag_current take TagId or AssetId only. The model was looping on
        //            search_sites (22 calls across 13 runs) with the station CODE, which
        //            search_sites cannot match - it matches SiteName. Only
        //            get_attribute_range needs a site, and the baseline is optional
        // 1.0.41.0 - REMOVE trend_get from the allowlist. 11 calls across every trace,
        //            all returning 45-50 bytes, ~4 attempts per run, each costing a turn
        //            that re-sends the whole conversation. Demotion was not enough
        // 1.0.40.0 - Follow-up chat answers "what is it now" with live_get /
        //            get_tag_current, not get_asset_tags and never history_get: a
        //            current-value question was pulling a whole time series
        // 1.0.39.0 - Allowlist get_tag_current / live_get: the 1.0.27.0 filter reached the
        //            follow-up chat and would have denied the live-value lookups the
        //            follow-up prompt asks for
        // 1.0.38.0 - Follow-up chat scoped to the asset: live-value questions now go
        //            search_assets -> get_asset_tags(AssetId) instead of a site-wide scan,
        //            and resolved ids are reused for the rest of the conversation
        // 1.0.37.0 - A failed OPTIONAL analysis (predict_* / trend_get) now tells the model
        //            explicitly not to cite it: its absence is not a limitation of the
        //            verdict, and reporting it made sound conclusions look under-evidenced
        // 1.0.36.0 - Operator-facing engine names (AiEngineBrand / AiEngineName1 / 2)
        //            replace the internal MCP1/MCP2 plumbing labels in the UI; logs and
        //            traces keep srv1/srv2 for diagnosis
        // 1.0.35.0 - Caveats must state a limitation that actually weakens THIS verdict; a
        //            source that was not needed (REDA logs, a failed optional ML call) is
        //            not a caveat and made sound verdicts look under-evidenced
        // 1.0.34.0 - Allowlist the ML analyses predict_track_health / predict_pm_operation /
        //            predict_pm_cluster (cap 1 each, evidence-class not history-class) and
        //            tell the model when to use them: track leakage type locates the fault
        //            electrically and major_events correlate with the incidence time
        // 1.0.33.0 - Coherence findings are reported as OBSERVATIONS, never as a diagnosis
        //            that a sensor is faulty (telemetry cannot establish that, and the claim
        //            carries liability). Incoherent data now yields INCONCLUSIVE, not
        //            NOT_CONFIRMED -- the latter would assert the asset is sound
        // 1.0.32.0 - SENSOR HEALTH FIRST: check timestamp coherence, physical plausibility,
        //            coupled movement, frozen data and recovery shape before concluding a
        //            field fault -- a failing sensor and a failing asset give the same value
        // 1.0.31.0 - Status reports promptCache state, scope and how to verify it
        // 1.0.30.0 - Fix CS0165: 'raw' was read by the instrumentation finally block
        //            before definite assignment, so every build needed a manual edit
        // 1.0.29.0 - Batch B complete: single cache_control marker on the SYSTEM block
        //            (covers tools + system, 87% of the fixed prompt) via
        //            AnthropicClient 1.0.1.0; the tools-block marker is dropped as
        //            redundant. Still default OFF -- confirm meta.tokensCacheRead
        // 1.0.28.0 - Batch B (partial): optional cache_control on the tools block
        //            (AnthropicPromptCache, default OFF) -- caches ~2,000 tok/turn that
        //            the trace showed being re-sent at full price on every turn.
        //            System-block caching still needs AnthropicClient.cs
        // 1.0.27.0 - Batch A: tool schemas filtered on BOTH paths (was 28/turn on SSE);
        //            METHOD block moved from the per-alert user message into the system
        //            prompt (cacheable share 42% -> 87%); trend_get demoted out of the
        //            history family and marked supplementary; get_asset_tags named the
        //            authoritative TagId source; attribute rows compacted to short keys
        //            with a legend (~55% smaller)
        // 1.0.26.0 - Status reports the log directory, write permission, counters and
        //            the last logging error. A swallowed write failure previously made
        //            "no logs anywhere" impossible to diagnose
        // 1.0.25.0 - Greppable leveled log ai-log-YYYYMMDD.txt (INFO/WARN/ERROR) across
        //            REQ/MCP/TOOL/GROUND/VERDICT/LIFE; daily rotation with background
        //            gzip of older files, retention over the archives, drop counters
        // 1.0.24.0 - Deep instrumentation: exact bytes sent/received per model turn,
        //            REAL token usage from the reply (incl. cache read/write), per
        //            tool-call timing, args, raw vs kept size, narrowed/truncated
        //            flags and reject reason; totals in meta and the envelope trace
        // 1.0.23.0 - get_attribute_range is SITE-scoped server-side (~266KB, then
        //            truncated and discarded). Narrow the result to the AssetIds this
        //            analysis is actually using, client-side
        // 1.0.22.0 - Narrowing guidance was tool-wrong: history_get declares TagId and
        //            NOT AttributeId, trend_get the reverse. An undeclared identifier is
        //            stripped before the call, leaving AssetId alone -> every tag on the
        //            asset -> 103KB reply. State the identifier per tool
        // 1.0.21.0 - Require history calls to name ONE attribute (TagId/AttributeId).
        //            Measured: whole-asset month = 206KB track / 862KB signal / 12MB
        //            point machine, all cut in half in transit; one tag over the window
        //            is 1-12KB and arrives intact
        // 1.0.20.0 - The MCP client splices "[...N chars truncated]" into the MIDDLE of
        //            large JSON results, so head and tail parsed but the whole did not.
        //            Salvage and repair the head instead of discarding the payload
        // 1.0.19.0 - Operational filter was replacing factual EVIDENCE lines: it matched
        //            ordinary words (reset / should / must). Split it -- movement
        //            directives are blocked everywhere, advisory words only in
        //            recommended_action
        // 1.0.18.0 - Tool results arrive as a TRUNCATED document followed by a COMPLETE
        //            one on a later line; the sequential reader aborted on the broken
        //            first document and discarded intact telemetry. Recover
        //            line-delimited documents. Context quote now resolves line+position
        // 1.0.17.0 - Salvage the verdict object when the model wraps it in prose or a
        //            fence, instead of discarding a good verdict over packaging;
        //            report the REAL parser message and the characters at its
        //            position so payload corruption is identified, not guessed
        // 1.0.16.0 - Tool results can arrive as SEVERAL concatenated JSON documents
        //            (one per MCP content block). A single-document parse rejected
        //            the lot, so complete, well-formed telemetry was discarded as
        //            malformed. Parse permissively and judge each document
        // 1.0.15.0 - Evidence limit 500 -> 200 (configurable): a 500-sample series
        //            overran MaxToolResultChars, was truncated, and truncated JSON
        //            cannot parse -- so the richest evidence was being discarded.
        //            toolTrace now reports a reject reason and the payload tail
        // 1.0.14.0 - Evidence gate accepted only top-level data keys or top-level numbers,
        //            so the FRS tools' NESTED payloads were rejected as ungrounded even
        //            though they carry telemetry; accept substantive nested content.
        //            toolTrace now shows a preview of anything still rejected
        // 1.0.13.0 - Allowlist the FRS (MCP2) tools analyse_alert / get_hist_realtime /
        //            fetch_alert_details_frs. They were filtered out of verdict mode, so
        //            the model never saw the tools built for alert analysis and could
        //            never satisfy the history-evidence gate
        // 1.0.12.0 - Hand the model an explicit EdgeX-format (ddMMyyyy_HHmmss) analysis
        //            window; add per-tool outcome trace to meta so "ungrounded" names the
        //            call that returned nothing; history-family cap 2 -> 3
        // 1.0.11.0 - ProduceVerdictJsonAsync: in-process entry point so another
        //            controller can get a verdict without the site calling itself
        // 1.0.10.0 - Fix SSE word-gluing: boundary space was lost between text chunks
        //            ("threshold4.67"); streaming verdict text now reads correctly
        // 1.0.9.0 - viz narrative: trigger_pct / recovery_pct / phase_note + secondary.unit
        //           so the chart shows healthy -> degrade -> trigger -> recovery
        // 1.0.8.0 - Evidence quality: history calls get full scale (limit cap 10 -> 500,
        //           the API max) now that compact columnar output makes it affordable
        // 1.0.7.0 - Latency: cache MCP tool discovery (was re-fetched every request);
        //           send only allowlisted tool schemas to the model in verdict mode
        // 1.0.6.0 - AnalyzeAlertJson service endpoint (single-JSON verdict envelope),
        //           analyze trace log, tool budget + read-only allowlist, grounding gate,
        //           schema-driven tool args, columnar evidence output
        // 1.0.5.0 - AlertLive AI-analyze URL fix (@Url.Action); prompt speed/terseness pass;
        //           window-naming rule (no day-count on averages); viz block for the chart
        // 1.0.4.0 - Follow-up chat in the diagnostic popup (AnalyzeChat)
        // 1.0.3.0 - Preview: site-wise triage scheme
        // 1.0.2.0 - Verdict reframe + main-page polish
        // 1.0.1.0 - UI redesign
        // 1.0.0.0 - Per-alert AI verdict via AiChat/AnalyzeAlert + MCP

        private static readonly int _maxIter = ReadInt("MaxIter", 10);
        private static readonly int _maxHistory = ReadInt("MaxHistoryTurns", 6);
        private static readonly int _maxToolLen = ReadInt("MaxToolResultChars", 20000);
        private static readonly int _warnTokens = ReadInt("WarnTokenThreshold", 40000);
        // v1.0.160.194: chat-loop bounds. Applied to the CHAT path only (rawJsonMode == false);
        // analyze keeps _maxIter unchanged. _chatLoopGuard is the master kill-switch (field revert);
        // when false, chat reverts to _maxIter and all guard branches below are skipped -- exactly .193.
        // Values are clamped so a bad config can never skip the loop or force-answer on turn 0.
        private static readonly int _chatMaxIter = Math.Max(2, ReadInt("ChatMaxIter", 40));
        private static readonly int _chatMaxWallSec = Math.Max(5, ReadInt("ChatMaxWallSec", 90));
        private static readonly bool _chatLoopGuard = ReadBool("ChatLoopGuard", true);
        // v1.0.160.195 (memory-loss B): self-heal follow-up-chat grounding from the stored analyze
        // input when the chat POST arrives without the alert card. Requires AiAuditDbEnabled (nothing
        // to read without it); degrades to prior behaviour on any miss. Default on; off = exactly .194.
        private static readonly bool _chatGroundBackfill = ReadBool("ChatGroundBackfill", true);

        // ── Tool logging ───────────────────────────────────────
        // Enable with: <add key="AiToolLoggingEnabled" value="true" />
        private static readonly bool _toolLoggingEnabled =
            ReadBool("AiToolLoggingEnabled", false);
        private static readonly int _maxToolLogChars =
            ReadInt("AiToolLogMaxChars", 20000);
        private static readonly object _toolLogLock = new object();
        private static readonly string _toolLogDir =
            System.IO.Path.Combine(
                AppDomain.CurrentDomain.BaseDirectory, "App_Data", "AiToolLogs");

        private static readonly Lazy<AnthropicClient> _ai =
            new Lazy<AnthropicClient>(CreateAiClient);

        // SYNTHESIS CLIENT. Same class, smaller max_tokens. The global 8096 is right
        // for follow-up chat and far too loose for a verdict object: an output ceiling
        // is the only hard control over the slowest phase of the analysis. Constructing
        // a second client avoids touching AnthropicClient's signature.
        private static readonly Lazy<AnthropicClient> _aiSynth =
            new Lazy<AnthropicClient>(CreateSynthesisClient);

        // ---- OpenAI provider -------------------------------------------------
        // OpenAiClient speaks OpenAI on the wire and returns ANTHROPIC-SHAPED JSON,
        // so the agentic loop, tool policy, grounding gate and verdict validation are
        // untouched by the switch. Selected per request, so the two can be compared
        // on the SAME alert rather than on different ones.
        //   <add key="OpenAiApiKey"  value="sk-..." />
        //   <add key="OpenAiModel"   value="gpt-5.4" />
        //   <add key="OpenAiBaseUrl" value="https://api.openai.com/v1" />
        private static readonly Lazy<OpenAiClient> _oai =
            new Lazy<OpenAiClient>(() => CreateOpenAiClient(ReadInt("AnthropicMaxTokens", 8096)));
        private static readonly Lazy<OpenAiClient> _oaiSynth =
            new Lazy<OpenAiClient>(() => CreateOpenAiClient(ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeSynthesisMaxTokens", 1200), 400, 4000)));
        // v1.0.134.0: DeepSeek provider (OpenAI-compatible). Branded "ENERGY7 TESLA 2".
        private static readonly Lazy<DeepSeekClient> _deepseek =
            new Lazy<DeepSeekClient>(() => CreateDeepSeekClient(ReadInt("DeepSeekMaxTokens", 8096)));
        private static readonly Lazy<DeepSeekClient> _deepseekSynth =
            new Lazy<DeepSeekClient>(() => CreateDeepSeekClient(ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeSynthesisMaxTokens", 1200), 400, 4000)));

        private static OpenAiClient CreateOpenAiClient(int maxTokens)
        {
            return new OpenAiClient(
                ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["OpenAiApiKey"],
                ReadStr("OpenAiModel", "gpt-5.4"),
                maxTokens,
                ReadStr("OpenAiBaseUrl", "https://api.openai.com/v1"));
        }

        private static DeepSeekClient CreateDeepSeekClient(int maxTokens)
        {
            // v1.0.135.0: thinking defaults OFF (DeepSeek V4 enables it by default server-side,
            // adding 30-80s hidden reasoning billed as output). DeepSeekThinking=true re-enables.
            return new DeepSeekClient(
                ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["DeepSeekApiKey"],
                ReadStr("DeepSeekModel", "deepseek-v4-pro"),
                maxTokens,
                ReadStr("DeepSeekBaseUrl", "https://api.deepseek.com/v1"),
                ReadBool("DeepSeekThinking", false));
        }

        // Default provider; a request may override it (UI toggle).
        private static readonly string _aiProviderDefault = ReadStr("AiProvider", "quantum10");   // v1.0.160.202: QUANTUM (DeepSeek Pro) is the default for everyone
        private string _provider;   // resolved per request
        // v1.0.160.42: per-request THINK toggle (UI checkbox -> ctx.think). null = not specified
        // by the request, in which case the DeepSeekThinking config default applies.
        private bool? _thinkReq;
        // v1.0.160.57: wisdom actually INJECTED into this run. Counted where the blocks are built,
        // because nothing else in the system records it -- Wisdom.cs logs only save/edit/approve.
        private int _wisDoctrinal, _wisField, _wisCircuit, _wisLearned, _wisChecklist, _wisChars;
        private string _driverSetStr;
        private int _bashCalls;   // v1.0.160.59: per-run bash budget
        // v1.0.160.63: prefetch tool work. _trToolCallCount counts only IN-LOOP calls, so an audit
        // built from it reported 0 for a run that made 8 prefetch calls.
        private int _trPrefetchCalls;
        // v1.0.160.68: raw prompt/response for the audit record.
        private string _lastPromptFull, _lastResponseFull;
        // v1.0.160.85: identity captured BEFORE the first await. HttpContext.Current is gone
        // after ConfigureAwait(false), so it cannot be read later in the run.
        private string _luName, _luEmail; private bool _luSiteKeep;
        private long _auditAnalysisId;   // v1.0.160.73: 0 = no row (Start failed or DB dormant)
        private DateTime _reqStartUtc = DateTime.UtcNow;

        // v1.0.134.0: three base providers. UI sends "anthropic" | "openai" | "deepseek"
        // (branded ENERGY7 NEXUS / ORION / QUANTUM). Normalize defensively.
        // v1.0.158.0: NEXUS/ORION model families. Each variant reuses the anthropic/openai
        // CLIENT but with its own model string (see AnalysisModelOverride). ProviderKind maps
        // every variant to its transport; _provider keeps the raw value for the model pick.
        //   nexus16 -> Anthropic Opus 4.6 | nexus19 -> Opus 4.8 | nexus49 -> Fable 5
        //   orion16 -> OpenAI GPT-5.6      | orion17 -> GPT-5.6 Sol
        private string ProviderKind
        {
            get
            {
                string p = (_provider ?? _aiProviderDefault ?? "anthropic").Trim().ToLowerInvariant();
                if (p.Contains("deep")) { return "deepseek"; }
                if (p == "orion16" || p == "orion17") { return "openai"; }   // ORION variants = OpenAI transport
                if (p == "nexus16" || p == "nexus19" || p == "nexus49") { return "anthropic"; }  // NEXUS variants = Anthropic transport
                // v1.0.160.9: bare BRAND labels. The app/API sends QUANTUM/NEXUS/ORION (brand),
                // not the provider value (deepseek/openai/anthropic). Without these a bare
                // "quantum" fell through to the final "anthropic" and ran on the Anthropic key.
                // Placed AFTER the numbered-variant checks so their model overrides are untouched;
                // v1.0.160.11: bare-brand match must be CONTAINS, not ==, or the full label the
                // picker sends ("ENERGY7 QUANTUM") fails the equality and falls through to the
                // anthropic default -- reintroducing the exact QUANTUM->anthropic bug. Contains
                // handles bare ("QUANTUM") AND prefixed ("ENERGY7 QUANTUM"/"tesla 2"). Numbered
                // variant checks above still run first, so their model overrides are untouched.
                // bare brands use each transport's base model (AnalysisModelOverride returns null).
                if (p.Contains("quantum") || p.Contains("tesla 2") || p.Contains("tesla2")) { return "deepseek"; }   // QUANTUM = DeepSeek transport
                if (p.Contains("orion") || p.Contains("tesla 1") || p.Contains("tesla1")) { return "openai"; }       // ORION = OpenAI transport
                if (p.Contains("nexus") || p.Contains("ultra")) { return "anthropic"; }                              // NEXUS = Anthropic transport
                if (p == "openai" || p == "gpt" || p.Contains("gpt")) { return "openai"; }
                return "anthropic";
            }
        }
        // v1.0.158.0: model-string override for the NEXUS/ORION variants. Returns null for the
        // base providers (NEXUS/ORION/QUANTUM use their configured default model). Each is
        // config-overridable so the exact model IDs can be corrected without a rebuild.
        private string AnalysisModelOverride
        {
            get
            {
                string p = (_provider ?? _aiProviderDefault ?? "").Trim().ToLowerInvariant();
                if (p == "nexus16") { return ReadStr("ModelNexus16", "claude-opus-4-6"); }
                if (p == "nexus19") { return ReadStr("ModelNexus19", "claude-opus-4-8"); }
                if (p == "nexus49") { return ReadStr("ModelNexus49", "claude-fable-5"); }
                if (p == "orion16") { return ReadStr("ModelOrion16", "gpt-5.6"); }
                if (p == "orion17") { return ReadStr("ModelOrion17", "gpt-5.6-sol"); }
                // v1.0.160.42: QUANTUM 1.1 = DeepSeek Flash. Config-overridable so the exact
                // model id can be corrected without a rebuild.
                if (p == "quantum11") { return ReadStr("ModelQuantum11", "deepseek-v4-flash"); }
                return null;
            }
        }
        private bool UseOpenAi { get { return ProviderKind == "openai"; } }
        private bool UseDeepSeek { get { return ProviderKind == "deepseek"; } }
        // v1.0.160.42: effective thinking state -- request toggle wins, else the config default.
        private bool ThinkOn { get { return _thinkReq.HasValue ? _thinkReq.Value : ReadBool("DeepSeekThinking", false); } }
        // v1.0.160.42: absent/blank ctx.think => null (fall back to the DeepSeekThinking config
        // default). Only an explicit true/1/on or false/0/off overrides it.
        private static bool? ParseThinkCtx(string v)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(v)) { return null; }
            string t = v.Trim().ToLowerInvariant();
            if (t == "true" || t == "1" || t == "on" || t == "yes") { return true; }
            if (t == "false" || t == "0" || t == "off" || t == "no") { return false; }
            return null;
        }

        private static AnthropicClient CreateSynthesisClient()
        {
            string key = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnthropicApiKey"];
            string model = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnthropicModel"];
            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(model)) { model = "claude-sonnet-4-6"; }
            return new AnthropicClient(key, model, ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeSynthesisMaxTokens", 1200), 400, 4000));
        }

        // ── MCP Server 1: direct HTTP POST (your existing RDPMS server) ──
        private static readonly Lazy<McpClient> _mcp =
            new Lazy<McpClient>(() =>
            {
                string url = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["McpServerUrl"];
                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(url))
                    throw new Exception("McpServerUrl missing in web.config");
                return new McpClient(url);
            });

        // ── MCP Server 2: standard SSE protocol (ngrok server) ──
        // v1.0.160.20: srv2 (MCP2) is used ONLY when McpServerUrl2 is configured (non-blank).
        // Absent or whitespace = srv2 DISABLED. Read once at startup; the URL's presence IS the
        // switch (no separate flag). Every _mcp2.Value access is guarded by this.
        private static readonly bool _srv2Enabled =
            !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["McpServerUrl2"]);

        private static readonly Lazy<McpSseClient> _mcp2 =
            new Lazy<McpSseClient>(() =>
            {
                string url = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["McpServerUrl2"];
                // Invariant defence: all callers are gated by _srv2Enabled, so this should not run
                // when srv2 is disabled. If a future unguarded access reaches here with no URL, fail
                // loudly rather than build a client on a blank endpoint.
                if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(url))
                    throw new InvalidOperationException("srv2 disabled (McpServerUrl2 not set)");
                return new McpSseClient(url.Trim());
            });

        // Tool routing map
        private static readonly Dictionary<string, int> _toolOwner =
            new Dictionary<string, int>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        private static readonly object _toolOwnerLock = new object();

        private class ToolLoadResult
        {
            public JArray Tools { get; set; }
            public int Count1 { get; set; }
            public int Count2 { get; set; }
            public string Error1 { get; set; }
            public string Error2 { get; set; }
            // per-request routing snapshot: immune to another request rebuilding
            // the shared _toolOwner dictionary mid-flight
            public Dictionary<string, int> OwnerMap { get; set; }
            // per-tool DECLARED argument names from the discovered inputSchema
            // (wire keys: "name" / "inputSchema" / "properties"). Used to inject
            // and keep ONLY arguments a tool actually accepts -- covers MCP2 too,
            // since it comes from discovery rather than hardcoded assumptions.
            public Dictionary<string, HashSet<string>> ArgMap { get; set; }
        }

        private static AnthropicClient CreateAiClient()
        {
            string key = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnthropicApiKey"];
            string model = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnthropicModel"] ?? "claude-sonnet-4-6";
            int tokens = ReadInt("AnthropicMaxTokens", 8096);
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(key))
                throw new Exception("AnthropicApiKey missing in web.config");
            return new AnthropicClient(key, model, tokens);
        }

        private static int ReadInt(string key, int def)
        {
            int v;
            return int.TryParse(ConfigurationManager.AppSettings[key], out v) ? v : def;
        }

        // v1.0.160.68: config double (pricing rates, fx).
        private static double ReadDbl(string key, double def)
        {
            string s2 = System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager.AppSettings[key];
            double v;
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s2)
                && double.TryParse(s2.Trim(), System.Globalization.NumberStyles.Float,
                                   System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, out v)) { return v; }
            return def;
        }

        private static bool ReadBool(string key, bool def)
        {
            string raw = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings[key];
            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(raw)) return def;
            raw = raw.Trim();
            return raw.Equals("true", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                || raw.Equals("1", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                || raw.Equals("yes", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                || raw.Equals("on", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        }

        private static int ResolveToolOwner(string toolName)
        {
            int owner = 1;
            lock (_toolOwnerLock)
            {
                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(toolName) && _toolOwner.ContainsKey(toolName))
                    owner = _toolOwner[toolName];
            }
            return owner;
        }

        // v1.0.160.193: instance recorder for the per-run timing/tag optimization trace. Called from the
        // response-phase LogToolEvent call-sites (which ARE instance context) -- LogToolEvent itself is
        // static and cannot touch these instance fields.
        private void RecordToolTiming(string toolName, JToken args, string result, int iteration, long elapsedMs)
        {
            if (elapsedMs < 0) { return; }
            if (elapsedMs > _trSlowestToolMs) { _trSlowestToolMs = elapsedMs; _trSlowestTool = toolName ?? ""; }
            if (!string.Equals(toolName, "history_get", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { return; }
            try
            {
                string tagId = null;
                string argsJson = args != null ? args.ToString(Formatting.None) : "";
                var mm = System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.Match(argsJson, "\"TagId\"\\s*:\\s*\"?(\\d+)");
                if (mm.Success) { tagId = mm.Groups[1].Value; }
                string attr = "";
                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(tagId)) { JObject md; lock (_trendLock) { _tagMeta.TryGetValue(tagId, out md); } if (md != null && md["attr"] != null) { attr = md["attr"].ToString(); } }
                JObject tf = new JObject();
                tf["tagId"] = tagId ?? "";
                tf["attr"] = attr;
                tf["ms"] = elapsedMs;
                tf["bytes"] = string.IsNullOrEmpty(result) ? 0 : result.Length;
                tf["iter"] = iteration;               // -1 = prefetch, >=0 = in agentic loop
                lock (_trendLock) { _trTagFetches.Add(tf); }
            }
            catch { }
        }

        private static void LogToolEvent(
            string conversationId,
            string phase,
            int iteration,
            string toolUseId,
            string toolName,
            int owner,
            JToken args,
            string result,
            Exception error,
            long elapsedMs)
        {
            if (!_toolLoggingEnabled) return;

            try
            {
                JObject entry = new JObject();
                entry["tsUtc"] = DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("o");
                entry["conversationId"] = conversationId ?? string.Empty;
                entry["phase"] = phase ?? string.Empty; // requested / response / error
                entry["iteration"] = iteration;
                entry["toolUseId"] = toolUseId ?? string.Empty;
                entry["toolName"] = toolName ?? string.Empty;
                entry["server"] = owner > 0 ? "srv" + owner : string.Empty;
                if (elapsedMs >= 0) entry["elapsedMs"] = elapsedMs;
                string argsJson = args == null
                    ? string.Empty
                    : CloneAndRedact(args).ToString(Formatting.None);

                entry["argsPreview"] = LimitForLog(argsJson, _maxToolLogChars);
                entry["resultLength"] = string.IsNullOrEmpty(result) ? 0 : result.Length;
                entry["resultPreview"] = LimitForLog(result, _maxToolLogChars);
                entry["error"] = error == null ? string.Empty : LimitForLog(error.ToString(), _maxToolLogChars);

                // v1.0.160.78: collect for AI_ALERT_McpCall. Only "response"/"error" phases -- a
                // "requested" entry has no latency or result yet and would double-count every call.
                // Reuses the values ALREADY redacted above rather than re-reading the raw args.
                if (_auditDbEnabled && (phase == "response" || phase == "error"))
                {
                    JObject mc = new JObject();
                    mc["Iteration"] = iteration < 0 ? 0 : iteration;
                    mc["ToolName"] = toolName ?? "";
                    mc["ToolCallId"] = toolUseId ?? "";
                    mc["ToolArgsJson"] = entry["argsPreview"];
                    mc["ToolResultJson"] = entry["resultPreview"];
                    mc["ToolResultLength"] = entry["resultLength"];
                    mc["McpServerName"] = owner > 0 ? ("srv" + owner) : "";
                    mc["CalledAtUtc"] = entry["tsUtc"];
                    if (elapsedMs >= 0) { mc["LatencyMs"] = elapsedMs; }
                    if (error != null) { mc["ErrorMessage"] = entry["error"]; }
                    McpCollect(conversationId, mc);
                }

                System.IO.Directory.CreateDirectory(_toolLogDir);
                string path = System.IO.Path.Combine(
                    _toolLogDir,
                    "ai-tool-" + DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd") + ".jsonl");

                lock (_toolLogLock)
                {
                    System.IO.File.AppendAllText(
                        path,
                        entry.ToString(Formatting.None) + Environment.NewLine,
                        Encoding.UTF8);
                }
            }
            catch (Exception logEx)
            {
                System.Diagnostics.Trace.TraceWarning(
                    "[AiChat] Tool log failed: " + logEx.Message);
            }
        }

        private static string LimitForLog(string text, int maxChars)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return string.Empty;
            text = RedactSecretText(text);
            if (maxChars <= 0 || text.Length <= maxChars) return text;
            return text.Substring(0, maxChars)
                + "\n...[truncated " + (text.Length - maxChars) + " chars]";
        }

        private static string RedactSecretText(string text)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(text)) return string.Empty;
            return Regex.Replace(
                text,
                @"(?i)(password|token|secret|api[_-]?key|authorization)\s*[:=]\s*[""']?[^,""'\s}]+",
                "$1=***REDACTED***");
        }

        private static JToken CloneAndRedact(JToken token)
        {
            if (token == null) return JValue.CreateNull();

            JObject obj = token as JObject;
            if (obj != null)
            {
                JObject copy = new JObject();
                foreach (JProperty prop in obj.Properties())
                {
                    if (IsSensitiveKey(prop.Name))
                        copy[prop.Name] = "***REDACTED***";
                    else
                        copy[prop.Name] = CloneAndRedact(prop.Value);
                }
                return copy;
            }

            JArray arr = token as JArray;
            if (arr != null)
            {
                JArray copy = new JArray();
                foreach (JToken item in arr)
                    copy.Add(CloneAndRedact(item));
                return copy;
            }

            return token.DeepClone();
        }

        private static bool IsSensitiveKey(string key)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(key)) return false;
            string k = key.ToLowerInvariant();
            return k.Contains("password")
                || k.Contains("token")
                || k.Contains("secret")
                || k.Contains("apikey")
                || k.Contains("api_key")
                || k.Contains("authorization");
        }

        // ── Training file ───────────────────────────────────────
        private static string _trainingCache = null;
        private static long _trainingMtime = 0;
        private static readonly object _trainLock = new object();
        private static readonly string _trainingPath =
            System.IO.Path.Combine(
                AppDomain.CurrentDomain.BaseDirectory, "App_Data", "training_.txt");

        private static string LoadTrainingText()
        {
            if (!System.IO.File.Exists(_trainingPath))
                return string.Empty;
            long mtime = new System.IO.FileInfo(_trainingPath).LastWriteTimeUtc.Ticks;
            lock (_trainLock)
            {
                if (_trainingCache != null && mtime == _trainingMtime)
                    return _trainingCache;
                string raw = System.IO.File.ReadAllText(_trainingPath, Encoding.UTF8).Trim();
                _trainingCache = string.IsNullOrEmpty(raw)
                    ? string.Empty
                    : "\n\n=== DOMAIN TRAINING ===\n" + raw + "\n=== END TRAINING ===";
                _trainingMtime = mtime;
                return _trainingCache;
            }
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  LOAD + MERGE TOOLS
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        // Tool discovery was re-run on EVERY request (2 x ListToolsAsync over
        // HTTPS for the same 22 schemas). Cached for AnalyzeToolCacheSec
        // (default 300). Only a GOOD result is cached -- a partial or failed
        // discovery is never stored, so an MCP outage cannot be pinned in.
        private static readonly int _toolCacheSec = ReadInt("AnalyzeToolCacheSec", 300);
        private static readonly object _toolCacheLock = new object();
        private static ToolLoadResult _toolCache;
        private static DateTime _toolCacheAt = DateTime.MinValue;

        private async Task<ToolLoadResult> LoadAllToolsAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken ct = default(System.Threading.CancellationToken))
        {
            ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
            if (_toolCacheSec > 0)
            {
                lock (_toolCacheLock)
                {
                    if (_toolCache != null
                        && (DateTime.UtcNow - _toolCacheAt).TotalSeconds < _toolCacheSec)
                    {
                        return _toolCache;
                    }
                }
            }
            ToolLoadResult r = new ToolLoadResult();
            r.Tools = new JArray();
            r.Error1 = null;
            r.Error2 = null;

            JArray tools1 = new JArray();
            try
            {
                tools1 = await AwaitWithCancel(WithClientLock(_mcp1Lock, () => _mcp.Value.ListToolsAsync(), ct, _jsonCapture != null), ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
                r.Count1 = tools1.Count;
            }
            catch (ClientBusyException) { throw; } // surfaces as HTTP 503 busy
            catch (OperationCanceledException ex)
            {
                if (ct.IsCancellationRequested) { throw; } // our cancel only
                r.Error1 = ex.Message; // ordinary client timeout: recoverable (rev2 parity)
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                r.Error1 = ex.Message;
            }

            ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested(); // no MCP2 discovery after cancel

            JArray tools2 = new JArray();
            // v1.0.160.20: discover srv2 only when configured. When disabled, tools2 stays empty
            // (Count2 defaults to 0, Error2 stays NULL) so srv2 tools never enter the model tool
            // list / OwnerMap / _toolOwner, nothing routes to owner 2, the srv1 discovery cache is
            // NOT invalidated (it skips when Error2 != null), and no [MCP2 error] is logged or
            // surfaced. Silent, as required. No else branch by design.
            if (_srv2Enabled)
            {
                try
                {
                    tools2 = await AwaitWithCancel(WithClientLock(_mcp2Lock, () => _mcp2.Value.ListToolsAsync(), ct, _jsonCapture != null), ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
                    r.Count2 = tools2.Count;
                }
                catch (ClientBusyException) { throw; } // surfaces as HTTP 503 busy
                catch (OperationCanceledException ex)
                {
                    if (ct.IsCancellationRequested) { throw; } // our cancel only
                    r.Error2 = ex.Message; // ordinary client timeout: recoverable (rev2 parity)
                }
                catch (Exception ex)
                {
                    r.Error2 = ex.Message;
                }
            }

            r.OwnerMap = new Dictionary<string, int>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            r.ArgMap = new Dictionary<string, HashSet<string>>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            HashSet<string> claimed = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            Action<JArray> mapArgs = (arr) =>
            {
                foreach (JToken tool in arr)
                {
                    string tn = tool["name"] != null ? tool["name"].ToString() : null;
                    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(tn) || claimed.Contains(tn)) { continue; }
                    claimed.Add(tn); // claim on FIRST server seen, matching OwnerMap precedence,
                                     // so MCP2 can never supply a schema for an MCP1-owned tool
                    // Only record a tool when discovery actually supplied a
                    // properties object. Present-but-empty => strip everything.
                    // Absent => unknown schema => leave args untouched.
                    JToken sch = tool["inputSchema"] ?? tool["input_schema"];
                    JToken pr = (sch != null && sch.Type == JTokenType.Object) ? sch["properties"] : null;
                    if (pr == null || pr.Type != JTokenType.Object) { continue; }
                    HashSet<string> props = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
                    foreach (var pp in ((JObject)pr).Properties()) { props.Add(pp.Name); }
                    r.ArgMap[tn] = props;
                }
            };
            mapArgs(tools1); mapArgs(tools2);
            foreach (JToken tool in tools1)
            {
                string name = tool["name"] != null ? tool["name"].ToString() : null;
                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) && !r.OwnerMap.ContainsKey(name)) { r.OwnerMap[name] = 1; }
            }
            foreach (JToken tool in tools2)
            {
                string name = tool["name"] != null ? tool["name"].ToString() : null;
                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) && !r.OwnerMap.ContainsKey(name)) { r.OwnerMap[name] = 2; }
            }

            lock (_toolOwnerLock)
            {
                _toolOwner.Clear();
                foreach (JToken tool in tools1)
                {
                    string name = tool["name"] != null ? tool["name"].ToString() : null;
                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) && !_toolOwner.ContainsKey(name))
                    {
                        _toolOwner[name] = 1;
                        r.Tools.Add(tool);
                    }
                }
                foreach (JToken tool in tools2)
                {
                    string name = tool["name"] != null ? tool["name"].ToString() : null;
                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) && !_toolOwner.ContainsKey(name))
                    {
                        _toolOwner[name] = 2;
                        r.Tools.Add(tool);
                    }
                }
            }

            if (_toolCacheSec > 0 && r.Error1 == null && r.Error2 == null && r.Tools.Count > 0)
            {
                lock (_toolCacheLock) { _toolCache = r; _toolCacheAt = DateTime.UtcNow; }
            }
            return r;
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  ROUTE TOOL CALL
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        // The MCP/AI clients are static singletons whose thread-safety contract
        // is not in hand. Until their sources are supplied, calls to each client
        // are SERIALIZED here (conservative): correctness first, throughput later.
        // Disable only after certifying the clients: AnalyzeJsonSerializeClients=false.
        // Strict parse: only an explicit, well-formed "false" disables verdict-path
        // serialization. Any other value (including malformed) keeps it ENABLED.
        private static readonly bool _serializeClients = !string.Equals(
            (ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnalyzeJsonSerializeClients"] ?? "").Trim(),
            "false", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        private static readonly System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim _mcp1Lock = new System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim(1, 1);
        private static readonly System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim _mcp2Lock = new System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim(1, 1);
        private static readonly System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim _aiLock = new System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim(1, 1);

        // BOUNDED acquisition. A never-completing client call must not wedge
        // the client for the whole app (that hazard was introduced by the
        // unbounded lock in rev 10). If the lock cannot be taken within
        // AnalyzeJsonClientLockMs, the call proceeds WITHOUT serialization:
        // degraded isolation is strictly better than a global stall, and the
        // pre-rev10 behaviour was unserialized anyway.
        private static readonly int _clientLockMs = ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeJsonClientLockMs", 20000), 1000, 120000);
        private static int ClampCfg(int v, int lo, int hi) { return v < lo ? lo : (v > hi ? hi : v); }

        // v1.0.160.172 (Fix 3): cache the static per-asset range calls (safe bands / topology barely
        // change). Reused across every alert on the same asset, so it removes those calls from the
        // serialized prefetch entirely. Keyed by tool+args, so correctness is preserved; TTL-bounded.
        private static readonly int _prefetchCacheTtlSec = ClampCfg(ReadInt("PrefetchRangeCacheSec", 900), 0, 86400);
        private static readonly System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentDictionary<string, KeyValuePair<DateTime, string>> _prefetchCache
            = new System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentDictionary<string, KeyValuePair<DateTime, string>>();
        private static string PrefetchCacheKey(string tool, JObject args)
        {
            if (_prefetchCacheTtlSec <= 0) { return null; }
            if (!string.Equals(tool, "get_attribute_range", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                && !string.Equals(tool, "get_attribute_range_history", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { return null; }
            try { return tool + "|" + (args != null ? args.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None) : ""); }
            catch { return null; }
        }
        private static bool TryGetPrefetchCache(string key, out string val)
        {
            val = null;
            KeyValuePair<DateTime, string> e;
            if (_prefetchCache.TryGetValue(key, out e) && e.Key > DateTime.UtcNow) { val = e.Value; return true; }
            return false;
        }
        private static void SetPrefetchCache(string key, string val)
        {
            _prefetchCache[key] = new KeyValuePair<DateTime, string>(DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(_prefetchCacheTtlSec), val);
        }

        // v1.0.160.172 (Fix 4): per-call timeout + one retry. Applied ONLY when serialization is OFF
        // (parallel prefetch) -- there it caps the slowest call so one stalled tool cannot dominate the
        // batch. In serialized mode it is disabled, because a call legitimately waits up to
        // _clientLockMs for the lock and a timeout would kill queued calls prematurely.
        private static readonly int _prefetchTimeoutMs = ClampCfg(ReadInt("PrefetchCallTimeoutMs", 12000), 2000, 60000);
        private static readonly int _prefetchRetries = ClampCfg(ReadInt("PrefetchCallRetries", 1), 0, 3);
        internal class ClientBusyException : Exception
        {
            public ClientBusyException() : base("client busy") { }
        }

        // SCOPE (corrected in rev 12): serialization applies ONLY to the verdict
        // endpoint (mustOwn = true). Chat / AnalyzeAlert / follow-up / Status keep
        // their original unserialized behaviour -- adding a cross-endpoint lock was
        // my scope creep and it created the rev-10 stall hazard on features that
        // already worked. In verdict mode the lock is MANDATORY: if it cannot be
        // owned within the bounded wait the call is NOT made; the request returns
        // busy. No unserialized singleton call ever happens on that path.
        private static async Task<T> WithClientLock<T>(System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim gate, Func<Task<T>> body, System.Threading.CancellationToken ct, bool mustOwn)
        {
            if (!mustOwn || !_serializeClients) { return await body().ConfigureAwait(false); }
            bool taken = false;
            try
            {
                taken = await gate.WaitAsync(_clientLockMs, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
                if (!taken)
                {
                    System.Diagnostics.Trace.TraceWarning("[AiChat] verdict client lock timeout; refusing rather than running unserialized");
                    throw new ClientBusyException();
                }
                ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested(); // may have been cancelled while waiting
                return await body().ConfigureAwait(false);
            }
            finally
            {
                if (taken) { gate.Release(); }
            }
        }

        private async Task<string> CallToolRoutedAsync(string toolName, JToken toolArgs, System.Threading.CancellationToken ct = default(System.Threading.CancellationToken), int ownerOverride = 0)
        {
            bool mustOwn = _jsonCapture != null; // verdict mode only
            int owner = ownerOverride > 0 ? ownerOverride : ResolveToolOwner(toolName);

            // v1.0.160.200: the controller owns the E7 token. Fetch the LATEST generation (cached;
            // a login fires only on first use / TTL) and forward it to the MCP on this call so the
            // MCP uses THIS token, never its static startup one. Fetched OUTSIDE the client lock so
            // a login round-trip never holds _mcp1Lock/_mcp2Lock. Never throws: null means the MCP
            // falls back to its own token for this call -- logged, not fatal.
            string e7tok = await E7ApiToken.GetTokenAsync(ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
            if (e7tok == null && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(E7ApiToken.LastError))
            {
                AiLog("WARN", "E7TOKEN", E7ApiToken.LastError);
            }

            // McpClient and McpSseClient have the same method signature
            string __routedResult;
            if (owner == 2 && _srv2Enabled)
                __routedResult = await AwaitWithCancel(WithClientLock(_mcp2Lock, () => _mcp2.Value.CallToolAsync(toolName, toolArgs, _maxToolLen, e7tok), ct, mustOwn), ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
            else if (owner == 2)
                // v1.0.160.20: srv2 tool requested while srv2 is disabled. It should never be
                // advertised (tools2 empty), so this is defensive only: a clean unavailable result
                // (LooksUsableToolResult rejects an object carrying an "error") instead of touching
                // the disabled client.
                __routedResult = "{\"error\":\"tool unavailable (srv2 disabled)\"}";
            else
                // v1.0.160.59: per-run bash budget. Refused with a message the model can act on, so it
                // stops rather than retrying into the 18-iteration ceiling.
                if (string.Equals(toolName, "bash", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
                {
                    _bashCalls++;
                    if (_bashCalls > _bashMaxCalls)
                    {
                        AiLog("WARN", "BASH", "per-run cap reached (" + _bashMaxCalls + "); refusing further calls");
                        return "bash call budget exhausted for this analysis (" + _bashMaxCalls
                             + " calls). Conclude from the evidence already gathered; do not retry.";
                    }
                    AiLog("INFO", "BASH", "call " + _bashCalls + "/" + _bashMaxCalls + " during analysis");
                }
                __routedResult = await AwaitWithCancel(WithClientLock(_mcp1Lock, () => _mcp.Value.CallToolAsync(toolName, toolArgs, _maxToolLen, e7tok), ct, mustOwn), ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
            // v1.0.160.200: reactive path. The MCP reports E7 rejected the forwarded token ->
            // invalidate it so the NEXT tool call re-logs in (single-flight). No in-place retry:
            // this call returns the MCP's error result, which the loop already treats as unusable,
            // and every subsequent call carries a fresh token.
            if (e7tok != null && IsE7SessionExpired(__routedResult))
            {
                E7ApiToken.Invalidate();
                AiLog("WARN", "E7TOKEN", "E7 session expired on '" + toolName + "'; token invalidated, next call re-logs in");
            }

            // v1.0.146.0: single funnel for ALL tool calls (prefetch + loop + chat) --
            // harvest identity + real trend here so every path contributes.
            TryHarvestGrounding(toolName, __routedResult);
            TryHarvestTrend(toolName, toolArgs, __routedResult);
            return __routedResult;
        }

        // v1.0.160.200: recognizes the marker the MCP server returns when E7 rejects the forwarded
        // token (contract: the MCP emits "e7_session_expired" on an E7 401/403). Marker-only on
        // purpose -- generic "403"/"forbidden" text is NOT matched, so an unrelated permission
        // error can never churn logins.
        private static bool IsE7SessionExpired(string toolResult)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(toolResult))
            {
                return false;
            }
            return toolResult.IndexOf("e7_session_expired", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) >= 0;
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  GET /AiChat/Status
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        [HttpGet]
        public async Task<ActionResult> Status()
        {
            // v1.0.160.107 -- F1-response. Privilege FIRST (CaptureLoginUser populates the identity
            // fields AiDebugAllowed reads, and both must run before the first await). A
            // non-privileged caller learns only whether the assistant is usable: no tool counts, no
            // mcp topology, no client-library name, no raw exception text.
            CaptureLoginUser();
            bool priv = AiDebugAllowed();
            try
            {
                ToolLoadResult loaded = await LoadAllToolsAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
                if (!priv)
                {
                    return Json(loaded.Tools.Count > 0
                        ? (object)new { ok = true }
                        : (object)new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
                }
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: booleans, not error text. No redaction attempt -- redaction is
                // open-ended and leaks eventually; the raw errors stay in the server log only.
                return Json(new
                {
                    ok = loaded.Tools.Count > 0,
                    version = ComponentVersion,
                    tools = loaded.Tools.Count,
                    mcp1 = new { tools = loaded.Count1, healthy = (loaded.Error1 == null) },
                    mcp2 = new { tools = loaded.Count2, healthy = (loaded.Error2 == null) },
                    promptCache = new
                    {
                        enabled = _promptCache,
                        scope = "tools + system prefix (one cache_control marker on the system block)",
                        verifyWith = "meta.tokensCacheRead on the next analysis -- non-zero means it is working"
                    },
                    logging = LogDiagnostics()
                }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: ex.Message never leaves the server, at ANY privilege.
                AiLog("WARN", "STATUS", "status failed: " + ex.Message);
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  GET /AiChat/Status2
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        // v1.0.160.116 CUT G3: batch verdict-state lookup for the alert board. Display only.
        [HttpPost]
        public ActionResult VerdictStates()
        {
            CaptureLoginUser();
            _roleSiteKeep = AiDebugAllowed();
            try
            {
                string body;
                using (System.IO.StreamReader sr = new System.IO.StreamReader(Request.InputStream, Encoding.UTF8))
                { body = sr.ReadToEnd(); }
                JObject payload = JObject.Parse(body ?? "{}");
                JArray ids = payload["alertIds"] as JArray;
                if (ids == null || ids.Count == 0)
                { return Json(new { ok = true, states = new JObject() }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet); }
                // Bounded: one page of the board, not an open-ended sweep of the alert table.
                List<long> list = new List<long>();
                for (int i = 0; i < ids.Count && list.Count < 200; i++)
                {
                    long v;
                    if (long.TryParse(ids[i].ToString(), out v) && v > 0) { list.Add(v); }
                }
                string engine = payload["engine"] != null ? payload["engine"].ToString() : "";
                JObject states = ListVerdictStates(list, engine, _roleSiteKeep);
                return Content(new JObject { { "ok", true }, { "states", states } }.ToString(Formatting.None),
                               "application/json");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // Never ex.Message to a browser (H4). A list that cannot resolve states must degrade
                // to "not_analyzed", not break the board.
                AiLog("WARN", "VERDICT_STATES", "batch state lookup failed: " + ex.Message);
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
        }

        // v1.0.160.184: per-operation rows for the popup's PM Analysis visuals, from the SAME
        // API the Point Machine Operation page's Model 4 uses -- HistorianApiBaseUrl +
        // api/pm4/analyze?SiteId&AssetId&WindowDays&AssetName&SiteName. (.183 called the
        // pm-operation-v4 route instead, which is a different surface.)
        // Same-origin on purpose: the analysis host must not be called from the browser.
        // Waveform arrays are dropped here -- a 30-day two-machine response carries current[] and
        // voltage[] on every op, which is megabytes; the visuals read only the fields in
        // PmOpKeepFields.
        [HttpGet]
        public async Task<ActionResult> PmOpsV4(string siteId, string assetId, int windowDays = 30,
            string assetName = "", string siteName = "", bool forceLive = false)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(assetId))
            {
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "assetId required" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }

            string baseUrl = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["HistorianApiBaseUrl"];

            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(baseUrl))
            {
                AiLog("ERROR", "PM_OPS", "HistorianApiBaseUrl is not configured");
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Analysis API not configured" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }

            string url = baseUrl.TrimEnd('/')
                       + "/api/pm4/analyze?SiteId=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(siteId ?? "")
                       + "&AssetId=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(assetId)
                       + "&WindowDays=" + windowDays
                       + "&AssetName=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(assetName ?? "")
                       + "&SiteName=" + Uri.EscapeDataString(siteName ?? "")
                       + (forceLive ? "&ForceLive=true" : "");

            System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch watch = System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch.StartNew();

            try
            {
                string raw;

                using (System.Net.Http.HttpClient http = new System.Net.Http.HttpClient())
                {
                    // ForceLive re-analyzes instead of serving the cache, so it needs the same
                    // headroom the Point Machine Operation page allows its own proxy.
                    http.Timeout = TimeSpan.FromMinutes(5);
                    raw = await http.GetStringAsync(url).ConfigureAwait(false);
                }

                JObject root = JObject.Parse(raw);
                int kept = SlimPmOps(root["a"] as JObject) + SlimPmOps(root["b"] as JObject);
                string body = root.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None);
                watch.Stop();

                AiLog("INFO", "PM_OPS", "pm4/analyze served for asset " + assetId
                    + " -- " + kept + " ops, " + raw.Length + " bytes in, " + body.Length + " bytes out, "
                    + watch.ElapsedMilliseconds + " ms" + (forceLive ? " (ForceLive)" : ""));

                return Content(body, "application/json");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                watch.Stop();
                AiLog("ERROR", "PM_OPS", "pm4/analyze fetch failed for asset " + assetId
                    + " after " + watch.ElapsedMilliseconds + " ms: " + SanitizeJsonError(ex.Message));
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
        }

        // v1.0.160.184: the only fields the four PM visuals read. Everything else on an op --
        // above all the current[]/voltage[] sample arrays -- is removed before the payload leaves
        // the server. cond_notes is kept (added .184): it carries the detector's own reasoning for
        // a flagged stroke, which is the one piece of an op worth reading in words.
        // Returns the op count so the caller can log what it served.
        private static readonly string[] PmOpKeepFields =
        {
            "time", "direction", "grade", "confirmed", "condition", "cond_notes", "fault_type", "reason",
            "features", "current"
        };

        // v1.0.160.185: a tile is ~96 px wide, so 40 points carry the stroke's shape exactly as
        // well as 486 do. Raising this raises the payload linearly -- see the .185 note above.
        private const int PmCurveMaxPoints = 40;

        private static void SlimPmCurve(JObject op)
        {
            JArray curve = op["current"] as JArray;

            if (curve == null)
            {
                return;
            }

            int count = curve.Count;

            if (count == 0)
            {
                op.Remove("current");
                return;
            }

            JArray sampled = new JArray();

            if (count <= PmCurveMaxPoints)
            {
                foreach (JToken point in curve)
                {
                    sampled.Add(PmCurvePoint(point));
                }
            }
            else
            {
                for (int i = 0; i < PmCurveMaxPoints; i++)
                {
                    int index = (int)((long)i * (count - 1) / (PmCurveMaxPoints - 1));
                    sampled.Add(PmCurvePoint(curve[index]));
                }
            }

            op["current"] = sampled;
        }

        private static double PmCurvePoint(JToken point)
        {
            double value;

            if (point == null || !double.TryParse(point.ToString(), out value))
            {
                return 0;
            }

            return Math.Round(value, 2);
        }

        private static int SlimPmOps(JObject side)
        {
            if (side == null)
            {
                return 0;
            }

            JArray ops = side["ops"] as JArray;

            if (ops == null)
            {
                return 0;
            }

            foreach (JToken opToken in ops)
            {
                JObject op = opToken as JObject;

                if (op == null)
                {
                    continue;
                }

                List<string> dropNames = new List<string>();

                foreach (JProperty prop in op.Properties())
                {
                    if (Array.IndexOf(PmOpKeepFields, prop.Name) < 0)
                    {
                        dropNames.Add(prop.Name);
                    }
                }

                foreach (string dropName in dropNames)
                {
                    op.Remove(dropName);
                }

                SlimPmCurve(op);
            }

            return ops.Count;
        }

        [HttpGet]
        public async Task<ActionResult> Status2()
        {
            // v1.0.160.107 -- F1-response. This endpoint publishes the srv2 tool catalogue, which is
            // internal topology. Privilege FIRST, before any await: a non-privileged caller gets a
            // fixed 403 and NO tool discovery is performed at all (not merely withheld).
            CaptureLoginUser();
            if (!AiDebugAllowed())
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 403;
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Forbidden" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
            try
            {
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: no configuration-key names in a response -- "McpServerUrl2 not set"
                // told a caller both that srv2 exists and what the key is called.
                if (!_srv2Enabled)
                    return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
                JArray tools = await _mcp2.Value.ListToolsAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: tool NAMES only -- the full schemas describe every argument the
                // internal tool surface accepts.
                JArray names = new JArray();
                for (int i = 0; i < tools.Count; i++)
                {
                    JToken nm = tools[i] != null ? tools[i]["name"] : null;
                    if (nm != null) { names.Add(nm.ToString()); }
                }
                return Json(new { ok = true, tools = names }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: never ex.Message at any privilege -- it carries paths and hosts.
                AiLog("WARN", "STATUS2", "status2 failed: " + ex.Message);
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  GET /AiChat/WisdomAuthProbe  --  TEMPORARY (identity probe, v1.0.124.0)
        //  Purpose: capture what User.Identity actually is in THIS deployment, so the coming
        //  Wisdom authorization gate can be pinned to a real identity value rather than
        //  guessed. Web.config declares no <authentication>/<authorization>, so the principal
        //  must be observed at runtime. Gated by a SEPARATE appSettings key "WisdomAuthProbe"
        //  (its own key, unrelated to the point-machine work). Key absent/false -> 404. Never
        //  logs anonymous hits. Logs every authenticated hit (no dedup, so a swallowed AiLog
        //  write cannot silently block capture); same generic body for every case; the real
        //  result lives only in the server log line WISDOM_AUTH. REMOVE this action once the
        //  identity is captured and set WisdomAuthProbe=false.
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        [HttpGet]
        [OutputCache(NoStore = true, Duration = 0, VaryByParam = "*")]
        public ActionResult WisdomAuthProbe()
        {
            bool probeOn = string.Equals(
                (ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["WisdomAuthProbe"] ?? "").Trim(),
                "true", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            if (!probeOn)
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 404;
                return Content("", "text/plain");
            }

            System.Security.Principal.IIdentity identity = (User != null) ? User.Identity : null;
            if (identity == null || !identity.IsAuthenticated)
            {
                // No authenticated principal: log nothing, reveal nothing.
                return Content("probe completed", "text/plain");
            }

            // Log every authenticated hit (temporary endpoint; operator turns the key off
            // after capture). No one-shot dedup: AiLog swallows write failures, so marking an
            // identity "logged" before a failed write could silently prevent the retry the
            // probe exists for. Duplicate lines also reveal per-user/per-worker variance.
            AiLog("INFO", "WISDOM_AUTH",
                "isAuthenticated=" + identity.IsAuthenticated
                + " type=" + (identity.AuthenticationType ?? "")
                + " name=" + (identity.Name ?? "")
                + " principalType=" + ((User != null) ? User.GetType().FullName : "")
                + " identityType=" + identity.GetType().FullName);
            return Content("probe completed", "text/plain");
        }

        // v1.0.55.11: per-alert Tool trace. The verdict popup's "Tool trace" button calls this
        // with the run's conversationId (the sse-xxx traceId emitted as the "meta" SSE event) and
        // gets back JUST that alert's tool calls -- toolName, args, result preview, size, timing --
        // so an engineer can see what each tool was asked and what it returned, without downloading
        // the whole day's log. Read-only; filters the day's ai-tool jsonl by conversationId.
        [HttpGet]
        [OutputCache(NoStore = true, Duration = 0, VaryByParam = "*")]
        public ActionResult ToolTrace(string convId)
        {
            // v1.0.160.58: ToolTrace had NO authorisation. It returns every tool call, argument and
            // RAW RESULT for a run -- the one place platform/hardware detail can reach a railway
            // user. Gated on the same predicate as the rest of debug/tools.
            if (!AiDebugAllowed())
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 403;
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "tool trace is restricted to site-keeping users" },
                            JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
            try
            {
                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(convId))
                { return Json(new { ok = false, error = "no convId" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet); }

                // v1.0.158.1: the popup used to say "No tool calls logged for this run" for THREE
                // different causes -- logging switched off, no log file, or id not found -- which
                // reads as "this run made no tool calls" and sent people hunting the wrong bug.
                // Report the actual reason.
                if (!_toolLoggingEnabled)
                {
                    JObject off = new JObject();
                    off["ok"] = true; off["convId"] = convId; off["count"] = 0;
                    off["calls"] = new JArray(); off["logging"] = false;
                    off["reason"] = "logging_disabled";
                    return Content(off.ToString(Formatting.None), "application/json");
                }
                JArray calls = new JArray();
                string path = System.IO.Path.Combine(
                    _toolLogDir, "ai-tool-" + DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("yyyyMMdd") + ".jsonl");
                // also try yesterday (a run just before UTC midnight can straddle files)
                string pathY = System.IO.Path.Combine(
                    _toolLogDir, "ai-tool-" + DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(-1).ToString("yyyyMMdd") + ".jsonl");
                string[] files = { path, pathY };

                for (int fi = 0; fi < files.Length; fi++)
                {
                    if (!System.IO.File.Exists(files[fi])) { continue; }
                    string[] lines;
                    try
                    {
                        // open shared: today's file is being appended to concurrently
                        using (var fs = new System.IO.FileStream(files[fi], System.IO.FileMode.Open,
                            System.IO.FileAccess.Read, System.IO.FileShare.ReadWrite))
                        using (var sr = new System.IO.StreamReader(fs, Encoding.UTF8))
                        { lines = sr.ReadToEnd().Split('\n'); }
                    }
                    catch { continue; }

                    for (int i = 0; i < lines.Length; i++)
                    {
                        string ln = lines[i];
                        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(ln) || ln.IndexOf(convId, StringComparison.Ordinal) < 0) { continue; }
                        JObject o;
                        try { o = JObject.Parse(ln.Trim()); }
                        catch { continue; }
                        if (!string.Equals((string)o["conversationId"], convId, StringComparison.Ordinal)) { continue; }
                        // one row per tool call (the "response"/"error"/"denied" phase carries the result)
                        string phase = (string)o["phase"] ?? "";
                        if (phase == "requested") { continue; }   // skip the request-only echo; response row has both
                        JObject row = new JObject();
                        row["tool"] = (string)o["toolName"] ?? "";
                        row["phase"] = phase;
                        row["stage"] = (string.Equals((string)o["toolUseId"], "prefetch", StringComparison.Ordinal)) ? "prefetch" : "model";   // v1.0.158.2
                        row["server"] = (string)o["server"] ?? "";
                        row["iter"] = o["iteration"];
                        row["ms"] = o["elapsedMs"];
                        row["args"] = (string)o["argsPreview"] ?? "";
                        row["resultLen"] = o["resultLength"];
                        row["result"] = (string)o["resultPreview"] ?? "";
                        row["error"] = (string)o["error"] ?? "";
                        calls.Add(row);
                    }
                    // v1.0.158.1: do NOT stop after today's file -- a run straddling UTC midnight
                    // has rows in BOTH files and the tail was being dropped.
                }
                // v1.0.158.1: still nothing? the run may predate both files (retention keeps ~14
                // days) -- scan every retained tool log for this id before giving up.
                bool anyFile = System.IO.File.Exists(path) || System.IO.File.Exists(pathY);
                if (calls.Count == 0)
                {
                    string[] all;
                    try { all = System.IO.Directory.GetFiles(_toolLogDir, "ai-tool-*.jsonl"); }
                    catch { all = new string[0]; }
                    if (all.Length > 0) { anyFile = true; }
                    for (int fj = 0; fj < all.Length; fj++)
                    {
                        if (string.Equals(all[fj], path, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                            || string.Equals(all[fj], pathY, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { continue; }
                        string[] ln2;
                        try
                        {
                            using (var fs2 = new System.IO.FileStream(all[fj], System.IO.FileMode.Open,
                                System.IO.FileAccess.Read, System.IO.FileShare.ReadWrite))
                            using (var sr2 = new System.IO.StreamReader(fs2, Encoding.UTF8))
                            { ln2 = sr2.ReadToEnd().Split('\n'); }
                        }
                        catch { continue; }
                        for (int i2 = 0; i2 < ln2.Length; i2++)
                        {
                            string l2 = ln2[i2];
                            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(l2) || l2.IndexOf(convId, StringComparison.Ordinal) < 0) { continue; }
                            JObject o2;
                            try { o2 = JObject.Parse(l2.Trim()); }
                            catch { continue; }
                            if (!string.Equals((string)o2["conversationId"], convId, StringComparison.Ordinal)) { continue; }
                            string ph2 = (string)o2["phase"] ?? "";
                            if (ph2 == "requested") { continue; }
                            JObject r2 = new JObject();
                            r2["tool"] = (string)o2["toolName"] ?? ""; r2["phase"] = ph2;
                            r2["stage"] = (string.Equals((string)o2["toolUseId"], "prefetch", StringComparison.Ordinal)) ? "prefetch" : "model";
                            r2["server"] = (string)o2["server"] ?? ""; r2["iter"] = o2["iteration"];
                            r2["ms"] = o2["elapsedMs"]; r2["args"] = (string)o2["argsPreview"] ?? "";
                            r2["resultLen"] = o2["resultLength"]; r2["result"] = (string)o2["resultPreview"] ?? "";
                            r2["error"] = (string)o2["error"] ?? "";
                            calls.Add(r2);
                        }
                        if (calls.Count > 0) { break; }
                    }
                }

                JObject outp = new JObject();
                outp["ok"] = true;
                outp["convId"] = convId;
                outp["count"] = calls.Count;
                outp["calls"] = calls;
                outp["logging"] = true;
                if (calls.Count == 0) { outp["reason"] = anyFile ? "not_found" : "no_log_file"; }
                return Content(outp.ToString(Formatting.None), "application/json");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // v1.0.160.108 H4: this action is already 403-gated, but the rule is "no ex.Message
                // to a browser at ANY privilege" -- detail goes to the log.
                AiLog("WARN", "TOOLTRACE", "tool trace failed: " + ex.Message);
                return Json(new { ok = false, error = "Unavailable" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
            }
        }

        // Fail-closed identity resolver. UNUSED here (compiles, no caller); placed so the
        // Wisdom build reuses it verbatim for endpoint authorization.
        private string ResolveWisdomIdentity()
        {
            // 1) Real ASP.NET identity when the site has authentication wired.
            if (User != null && User.Identity != null
                && User.Identity.IsAuthenticated
                && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(User.Identity.Name))
            {
                return User.Identity.Name.Trim();
            }
            // 2) v1.0.130.0: this portal runs its own login (no <authentication>
            //    section), so User.Identity is anonymous for everyone. Fall back to
            //    the app session username under a CONFIG-NAMED key -- inert until
            //    WisdomIdentitySessionKey is set, so nothing changes by default.
            try
            {
                string key = System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["WisdomIdentitySessionKey"];
                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(key) && Session != null)
                {
                    object v = Session[key.Trim()];
                    string name = v == null ? null : Convert.ToString(v);
                    if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(name))
                    {
                        return name.Trim();
                    }
                }
            }
            catch { }
            // 3) v1.0.131.0: optional LAST-RESORT default identity (e.g. "ENERGY7")
            //    for portals with no per-user identity at all. Config-gated and off
            //    by default. NOTE: with this set, anyone who can reach the portal
            //    acts as this shared identity -- audit lines carry no per-user name.
            string defId = System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["WisdomDefaultIdentity"];
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(defId))
            {
                return defId.Trim();
            }
            return null;
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  POST /AiChat/DryRunTools?siteId=&assetId=&days=3&runs=1&includeMl=false
        //  v1.0.105.0: run the REAL read-only MCP tools the AI uses, server-side, for tool
        //  TRANSPORT/AVAILABILITY testing. Shares CallToolRoutedAsync with the verdict flow,
        //  but does NOT reproduce the full verdict pipeline (no ClampToolArgs, no
        //  NarrowAttributeRange, no evidence-grade validation, no per-request budgets) - so a
        //  green run proves the tools RESPOND with usable-looking data, NOT that the verdict
        //  path will accept every result. No verdict, no model call, no writes.
        //  AUTH: this is a BROWSER-FACING diagnostic (called from the authenticated Alert
        //  Analysis / Historian page, like AnalyzeAlert), so it does NOT use the service-to-
        //  service X-Internal-Api-Key (a browser cannot hold that secret). It is GATED by
        //  appSettings "EnableDryRunTools" (default OFF -> 403), a production kill-switch, and
        //  relies on the app-level authentication that protects those pages. For a stricter
        //  posture add [Authorize] (ideally a diagnostic/admin role) to this action. Resource
        //  caps: runs 1-5, days 1-15, ML tools ONLY when includeMl=true (they are the slowest).
        //  Observes client-disconnect via Response.ClientDisconnectedToken.
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        [HttpPost]
        public async Task<ActionResult> DryRunTools(string siteId, string assetId, int days = 3, int runs = 1, bool includeMl = false)
        {
            // GATE - appSettings "EnableDryRunTools" must be "true". Default OFF: production
            // ships with the endpoint disabled (403), a server-side kill-switch matching the
            // client AA_DEBUG_TOOLS flag. This is a browser-facing diagnostic (called from the
            // authenticated Alert Analysis / Historian page, same as AnalyzeAlert), so it relies
            // on the app-level auth that protects those pages rather than the service-to-service
            // X-Internal-Api-Key (which a browser cannot hold). Hard resource caps below still
            // apply whenever it is enabled.
            string enableFlag = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["EnableDryRunTools"];
            if (!string.Equals(enableFlag, "true", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            { Response.StatusCode = 403; return Json(new { ok = false, error = "DryRunTools disabled (set EnableDryRunTools=true in appSettings to enable)" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet); }

            if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(assetId))
            { Response.StatusCode = 400; return Json(new { ok = false, error = "assetId required" }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet); }
            if (days < 1) { days = 1; } if (days > 15) { days = 15; }
            if (runs < 1) { runs = 1; } if (runs > 5) { runs = 5; }   // capped low for production

            System.Threading.CancellationToken ct = default(System.Threading.CancellationToken);
            try { ct = Response.ClientDisconnectedToken; } catch { }

            var log = new List<string>();
            var summary = new Dictionary<string, DryRunAgg>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            Action<string> Line = delegate(string s) { log.Add("[" + DateTime.Now.ToString("HH:mm:ss.fff") + "] " + s); };

            ToolLoadResult loaded;
            try { loaded = await LoadAllToolsAsync().ConfigureAwait(false); }
            catch (Exception ex) { return Json(new { ok = false, error = "tool load failed: " + ex.Message }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet); }

            DateTime now = DateTime.Now;
            DateTime start = now.AddDays(-days);
            string sd = start.ToString(_ddFmt), ed = now.ToString(_ddFmt);

            // The read-only tools the AI actually uses, with real args. get_attribute_range
            // needs a SiteId. ML tools are the SLOWEST and run ONLY when includeMl=true.
            var plan = new List<Tuple<string, JObject, bool>>
            {
                Tuple.Create("get_asset_tags",    NewArgs("AssetId", assetId), false),
                Tuple.Create("history_get",       HistWindowArgs("AssetId", assetId, start, now, _limitCapEvidence, "columnar"), false),
                Tuple.Create("get_hist_realtime", NewArgs("AssetId", assetId), false),
            };
            if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(siteId))
            {
                // v1.0.160.6: scope to AssetId when available. get_attribute_range is SITE-scoped
                // server-side (~266KB, truncated to ~12KB in transit -> the needed baseline can be
                // in the DROPPED part). Adding AssetId makes the server return just this asset's
                // ranges (~3KB, COMPLETE, no truncation) -- proven on the wire: {SiteId:14}=12083B
                // truncated vs {SiteId:14,AssetId:1607}=2968B intact. Falls back to SiteId-only when
                // assetId is blank.
                JObject rangeArgs = NewArgs("SiteId", siteId);
                string arAsset = GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "assetId");
                if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(arAsset)) { rangeArgs["AssetId"] = arAsset; }
                plan.Add(Tuple.Create("get_attribute_range", rangeArgs, false));
            }
            else
            {
                // v1.0.160.151: siteId is what BOTH failing tools depend on, by two different
                // routes: get_attribute_range is not PLANNED AT ALL without it (this branch), and
                // get_frs_alerts IS planned but built with NewFrsAlertsProbeArgs(siteId, ...), so an
                // empty siteId sends an empty SiteIds array and the server returns nothing.
                // One blank field, two tools, and the four downstream symptoms
                // ("configured envelope unavailable", no average markers, blank assetType,
                // "Still active" on a cleared alert) all follow from that single fact with nothing
                // saying so. This is the difference between a tool that FAILED and a tool that was
                // never CALLED, which is the distinction the whole day kept turning on.
                AiLog("WARN", "PREFETCH", "siteId is EMPTY -- get_attribute_range and get_frs_alerts "
                    + "were NOT CALLED. Envelopes, averages, assetType and resetTime all depend on "
                    + "them; expect 'configured envelope unavailable' and 'Still active'. "
                    + "assetId=" + Trunc(GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "assetId"), 20)
                    + " alertId=" + Trunc(GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "alertId"), 20));
            }
            // v1.0.118.0: get_frs_alerts declares SiteIds/AssetIds as ARRAYS (required: SiteIds),
            // per the MCP1 tools/list. The old singular NewArgs("SiteId",...) sent an unknown arg
            // and omitted the required SiteIds, so this probe failed. Build the correct array shape.
            plan.Add(Tuple.Create("get_frs_alerts", NewFrsAlertsProbeArgs(siteId, assetId), true));
            if (includeMl && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(siteId))
            {
                plan.Add(Tuple.Create("predict_track_health", NewPredictArgs("predict_track_health", siteId, assetId), true));
                plan.Add(Tuple.Create("predict_pm_operation", NewPredictArgs("predict_pm_operation", siteId, assetId), true));
            }

            Line("=================================================================");
            Line("DRY-RUN (server-side, real MCP tools) asset=" + assetId + " site=" + (siteId ?? "-")
                + " window=" + days + "d runs=" + runs + " ml=" + includeMl + " toolsLoaded=" + loaded.Tools.Count);

            for (int run = 1; run <= runs; run++)
            {
                Line("----- run " + run + "/" + runs + " -----");
                foreach (var step in plan)
                {
                    if (ct.IsCancellationRequested) { Line("  (client disconnected - aborting)"); break; }
                    string toolName = step.Item1; JObject toolArgs = step.Item2; bool optional = step.Item3;
                    var sw = System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch.StartNew();
                    DryRunAgg a = summary.ContainsKey(toolName) ? summary[toolName] : (summary[toolName] = new DryRunAgg());
                    string res = null; string err = null; bool ok = false;
                    try
                    {
                        res = await CallToolRoutedAsync(toolName, toolArgs, ct).ConfigureAwait(false);
                        ok = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(res) && LooksUsableToolResult(res, false);
                        if (!ok && string.IsNullOrEmpty(err)) { err = res == null ? "null result" : "unusable/empty result"; }
                    }
                    catch (Exception ex) { err = ex.Message; }
                    sw.Stop();
                    int bytes = res != null ? res.Length : 0;
                    string shape = res != null ? DryRunShape(res) : "";
                    a.Calls++; if (ok) a.Ok++; else a.Fail++; a.Ms.Add((int)sw.ElapsedMilliseconds); a.Bytes.Add(bytes); a.Shapes.Add(shape);
                    string flag = ok ? "OK " : (optional ? "opt" : "ERR");
                    Line("  [" + flag + "] " + toolName.PadRight(26) + " " + ((int)sw.ElapsedMilliseconds).ToString().PadLeft(6) + "ms "
                        + bytes.ToString().PadLeft(8) + "b  " + shape + (err != null ? ("  <" + Trunc(err, 120) + ">") : ""));
                }
                if (ct.IsCancellationRequested) { break; }
            }
            Line("DRY-RUN done.");

            var summaryOut = new List<object>();
            bool allStable = true;
            foreach (var kv in summary)
            {
                var a = kv.Value;
                int avg = a.Ms.Count > 0 ? (int)a.Ms.Average() : 0;
                int avgB = a.Bytes.Count > 0 ? (int)a.Bytes.Average() : 0;
                bool stable = a.Shapes.Count == 1 && a.Fail == 0;
                if (!stable) { allStable = false; }
                summaryOut.Add(new
                {
                    tool = kv.Key, calls = a.Calls, ok = a.Ok, fail = a.Fail,
                    avgMs = avg, avgBytes = avgB, shapes = a.Shapes.Count,
                    stable = stable, msMin = a.Ms.Count > 0 ? a.Ms.Min() : 0, msMax = a.Ms.Count > 0 ? a.Ms.Max() : 0
                });
            }

            return Json(new
            {
                ok = true,
                version = ComponentVersion,
                debugAllowed = AiDebugAllowed(),   // v1.0.160.58: drives which controls the view offers
                asset = assetId, site = siteId, windowDays = days, runs = runs,
                toolsLoaded = loaded.Tools.Count,
                allStable = allStable,
                summary = summaryOut,
                log = log
            }, JsonRequestBehavior.AllowGet);
        }

        private sealed class DryRunAgg
        {
            public int Calls, Ok, Fail;
            public List<int> Ms = new List<int>();
            public List<int> Bytes = new List<int>();
            public HashSet<string> Shapes = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.Ordinal);
        }

        // v1.0.160.109 CUT A: the ONE history-window builder. Typed DateTime in, so the timezone
        // decision is made in exactly one place and cannot be re-derived (or forgotten) per call site.
        //
        // EdgeX MCP `history_get` RELABELS the naive ddMMyyyy_HHmmss string as UTC
        // (MCPHelper.Compact.cs L56-57: SpecifyKind(start, DateTimeKind.Utc)) instead of converting,
        // which shifted every window +5.5 h. Its sibling tools (summary_get, gated_get,
        // get_attribute_range_history) take a naive DateTime and are CORRECT -- so the compensation
        // must be applied HERE, to history_get only. Compensating globally would break the others.
        // Flip HistGetSendsUtc to false the moment EdgeX ships Kind.Local, or the window shifts
        // -5.5 h instead of +5.5 h.
        private static readonly bool _histGetSendsUtc = ReadBool("HistGetSendsUtc", true);
        // NOTE: reuses the existing _istOffset (declared near ToEpochIst) -- it was added for exactly
        // this reason ("ToUniversalTime() silently used the SERVER's timezone"). Do not redeclare it.

        private static string HistStamp(DateTime ist)
        {
            // EXPLICIT IST -> UTC. Never ToUniversalTime(): that uses the AiChat host's locale, which
            // is not necessarily the EdgeX host's, and never Kind.Local for the same reason.
            DateTime t = _histGetSendsUtc ? ist - _istOffset : ist;
            return t.ToString(_ddFmt);
        }

        private static JObject HistWindowArgs(string key, string val, DateTime fromIst, DateTime toIst,
            int limit, string outputMode)
        {
            JObject o = NewArgs(key, val);
            o["StartDate"] = HistStamp(fromIst);
            o["EndDate"] = HistStamp(toIst);
            o["limit"] = limit;
            // outputMode is a PARAMETER, not a constant: the AssetId probe needs JSON because
            // PickAlertingTagId scans the response for the literal field name "TagID".
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(outputMode)) { o["outputMode"] = outputMode; }
            // v1.0.160.38: under a row cap keep the NEWEST rows -- the incident sits near the END of
            // the window. Omitting this is what made the derived-component fetch read a 32 h stale
            // sample as if it were the value at the alert.
            o["sort"] = "desc";
            return o;
        }

        // Per-run fetch cache. The KEY MUST carry the full shape: two callers wanting the same window
        // in different shapes (json vs columnar, limit 1 vs 5000) are NOT interchangeable.
        private readonly Dictionary<string, string> _histCache = new Dictionary<string, string>();

        private static string HistCacheKey(JObject args)
        {
            if (args == null) { return ""; }
            string tgt = args["TagId"] != null ? ("T" + args["TagId"])
                       : (args["AssetId"] != null ? ("A" + args["AssetId"]) : "?");
            return tgt + "|" + (args["StartDate"] != null ? args["StartDate"].ToString() : "")
                 + "|" + (args["EndDate"] != null ? args["EndDate"].ToString() : "")
                 + "|" + (args["limit"] != null ? args["limit"].ToString() : "")
                 + "|" + (args["sort"] != null ? args["sort"].ToString() : "")
                 + "|" + (args["outputMode"] != null ? args["outputMode"].ToString() : "");
        }

        // Single entry point for every history_get fetch: dedupes identical requests within a run and
        // checks the window the server actually applied.
        private async Task<string> HistFetchAsync(JObject args, ToolLoadResult loaded,
            System.Threading.CancellationToken ct, bool quiet = false)
        {
            string key = HistCacheKey(args);
            string hit;
            if (key.Length > 0 && _histCache.TryGetValue(key, out hit))
            {
                _histCacheHits++;
                return hit;
            }
            string res = await SafeAwait(PrefetchCallAsync("history_get", args, loaded, ct, quiet)).ConfigureAwait(false);
            if (key.Length > 0) { _histCache[key] = res; }
            CheckHistWindowEcho(args, res);
            return res;
        }

        private int _histCacheHits;
        // v1.0.160.110 SL5: summed per-call tool ms. NOT a wall-clock share -- prefetch is concurrent,
        // so this CAN exceed the elapsed time of the phase. Reconciliation uses the wall-clock phase
        // figures below, never this.
        private long _trToolCallMsSum;
        private long _trPrefetchWallMs;
        private long _trInLoopWallMs;
        // v1.0.160.192: per-run slowest-tool tracking for the Log optimization summary
        private string _trSlowestTool;
        private long _trSlowestToolMs;
        private int _trDistinctTools;
        // v1.0.160.193: per-tag fetch tally for the Log -- which tag/attr was fetched, how long, how
        // big, and (at request_end) whether it was USED (in the driver set / trigger) or WASTED.
        private readonly List<JObject> _trTagFetches = new List<JObject>();
        // v1.0.160.110 SL6b: ANALYSIS turns only -- _trTurns counts BILLABLE calls including the
        // Hindi translation, so gating the prompt-cache warning on it fired on every bilingual
        // single-turn run. These two answer different questions and must not be conflated.
        private int _trAnalysisTurns;
        private bool _histSkewLogged;

        // The server echoes the from/to it actually used. If that disagrees with what we asked for,
        // the compensation or its configuration has failed and the evidence is for the wrong window.
        // Logged once per run; the decision to REJECT such a block is taken by the caller/verdict path.
        private void CheckHistWindowEcho(JObject args, string res)
        {
            if (_histSkewLogged || string.IsNullOrEmpty(res)) { return; }
            try
            {
                DateTime want;
                if (args == null || args["StartDate"] == null) { return; }
                if (!DateTime.TryParseExact(args["StartDate"].ToString(), _ddFmt,
                        System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
                        System.Globalization.DateTimeStyles.None, out want)) { return; }
                int i = res.IndexOf("\"from\"", StringComparison.Ordinal);
                if (i < 0) { return; }
                int c = res.IndexOf(':', i); if (c < 0) { return; }
                int e = c + 1; while (e < res.Length && (res[e] == ' ')) { e++; }
                int st = e; while (e < res.Length && (char.IsDigit(res[e]))) { e++; }
                long epoch;
                if (e <= st || !long.TryParse(res.Substring(st, e - st), out epoch)) { return; }
                DateTime got = new DateTime(1970, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc).AddSeconds(epoch);
                // v1.0.160.134: the echo is a UTC epoch; `want` is the IST WALL-CLOCK string we sent.
                // Comparing them directly was right only while we pre-converted to UTC
                // (HistGetSendsUtc=true). After the EdgeX 1.5.57.16 contract and the flag flip the
                // server reads our string as IST, so the comparison must add the IST offset. Without
                // this the assertion reports exactly the 330 min it was built to detect -- on windows
                // that are correct. It fired 7 times in one day's log. The check had to be flipped
                // WITH the flag; I flipped the flag and left the check behind.
                DateTime gotWall = _histGetSendsUtc ? got : got.Add(_istOffset);
                double diffMin = Math.Abs((gotWall - DateTime.SpecifyKind(want, DateTimeKind.Utc)).TotalMinutes);
                if (diffMin > 2)
                {
                    _histSkewLogged = true;
                    AiLog("WARN", "HIST_WINDOW_SKEW", "requested " + args["StartDate"]
                        + " but the server applied a window " + Math.Round(diffMin) + " min away"
                        + " (HistGetSendsUtc=" + _histGetSendsUtc + ") -- history evidence may be for the wrong period");
                }
            }
            catch { }
        }

        private static string Trunc(string s, int n)
        { return string.IsNullOrEmpty(s) ? "" : (s.Length <= n ? s : s.Substring(0, n) + "..."); }

        // Compact shape signature of a tool result, for cross-run stability comparison.
        private static string DryRunShape(string txt)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(txt)) { return "empty"; }
            try
            {
                JToken j = JToken.Parse(txt);
                if (j.Type == JTokenType.Array)
                {
                    JArray a = (JArray)j;
                    string keys = a.Count > 0 && a[0] is JObject
                        ? ":" + string.Join(",", ((JObject)a[0]).Properties().Take(6).Select(p => p.Name))
                        : "";
                    return "array[" + a.Count + "]" + keys;
                }
                if (j.Type == JTokenType.Object)
                {
                    JObject o = (JObject)j;
                    return "{" + string.Join(",", o.Properties().Take(8).Select(p =>
                        p.Name + "=" + (p.Value.Type == JTokenType.Array ? "arr" + ((JArray)p.Value).Count : p.Value.Type.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()))) + "}";
                }
                return j.Type.ToString().ToLowerInvariant();
            }
            catch
            {
                if (txt.TrimStart().StartsWith("<")) { return "html/" + txt.Length + "b"; }
                return "text/" + txt.Length + "b";
            }
        }

        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        //  POST /AiChat/Chat
        // ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        [HttpPost]
        public async Task<ActionResult> Chat()
        {
            // v1.0.160.107 -- pin 3: identity FIRST, before the body read.
            CaptureLoginUser();
            _roleSiteKeep = AiDebugAllowed();   // v1.0.160.108 H2: one role decision, pre-await
            string body;
            using (System.IO.StreamReader sr = new System.IO.StreamReader(Request.InputStream, Encoding.UTF8))
                body = await sr.ReadToEndAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);

            JArray messagesRaw;
            JObject chatPayload = null;
            try
            {
                chatPayload = JObject.Parse(body);
                messagesRaw = chatPayload["messages"] as JArray;
                if (messagesRaw == null) messagesRaw = new JArray();
            }
            catch
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return Content("Bad JSON", "text/plain");
            }

            if (messagesRaw.Count == 0)
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return Content("No messages", "text/plain");
            }

            Response.ContentType = "text/event-stream";
            Response.Headers["Cache-Control"] = "no-cache";
            Response.Headers["X-Accel-Buffering"] = "no";
            Response.Buffer = false;
            Response.BufferOutput = false;

            try
            {
                // v1.0.160.107 -- F7. FAIL CLOSED: refuse an instruction-extraction request BEFORE the
                // model and tools run, so no summary or paraphrase can be produced. Inside this try so
                // the finally below still emits [DONE] exactly once; EmptyResult because a bare return
                // cannot compile in Task<ActionResult>.
                if (IsInstructionExtractionRequest(LastRealUserText(messagesRaw)))
                {
                    WriteSse("text", new { text = FixedExtractionRefusal });
                    return new EmptyResult();
                }

                // v1.0.160.191: FOLLOW-UP CHAT GROUNDING. The chat used to call RunAgenticLoop with only
                // the messages, so the model re-discovered the alert every turn (search_sites ->
                // get_frs_alerts -> ...) and hit the step limit without answering. The web now sends the
                // SAME alert card (+ alertId/analysisId) it gave to analyze; we build a grounding system
                // prompt from that card PLUS the cause's FRS logic (CauseToLogic) so the model starts with
                // everything -- alert detail, thresholds, relays, resolved values, and the exact rule --
                // and answers in 1-2 steps instead of re-investigating.
                // v1.0.160.195 (memory-loss B): if the chat POST didn't carry the alert card, self-heal
                // the grounding from the stored analyze input (AlertInputJson) so the model starts grounded
                // and does not re-discover the alert and thrash to the step limit. Gated on
                // ChatGroundBackfill; on any miss groundPayload stays as chatPayload (prior behaviour).
                JObject groundPayload = chatPayload;
                if (_chatGroundBackfill && !ChatPayloadHasCard(chatPayload))
                {
                    JObject stored = LoadStoredAlertContext(chatPayload);
                    if (stored != null)
                    {
                        if (stored["alertId"] == null && chatPayload["alertId"] != null) { stored["alertId"] = chatPayload["alertId"]; }
                        if (stored["analysisId"] == null && chatPayload["analysisId"] != null) { stored["analysisId"] = chatPayload["analysisId"]; }
                        groundPayload = stored;
                        AiLog("INFO", "CHAT", "grounding self-healed from stored AlertInputJson (alertId=" + (chatPayload["alertId"] != null ? chatPayload["alertId"].ToString() : "?") + ")");
                    }
                }
                string chatGrounding = BuildChatGrounding(groundPayload);
                // v1.0.160.197: bind the point-machine operation averages into the grounding so chat
                // returns the last-operation voltage/current deterministically. Guidance alone wasn't
                // enough (live_get is unparseable by the model; predict_pm_operation can be down). PT* +
                // assetId only; "" on any miss -> the .196 guidance still applies.
                try
                {
                    string pmVals = BuildPmOperationValues(groundPayload);
                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(pmVals)) { chatGrounding = (chatGrounding ?? "") + pmVals; }
                }
                catch { }
                await RunAgenticLoop(messagesRaw, chatGrounding).ConfigureAwait(false);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                WriteSse("error", new { message = FriendlyError(ex) });
            }
            finally
            {
                try { Response.Write("data: [DONE]\n\n"); Response.Flush(); } catch { }
            }

            return new EmptyResult();
        }

        // POST /AiChat/AnalyzeAlert
        // Scoped single-alert analysis. Reuses the same MCP tools + agentic loop as Chat,
        // but with an analyze-specific system prompt and raw JSON output (no operational
        // filter, no out-of-scope gate). Streams the SAME SSE frames as Chat.
        [HttpPost]
        public async Task<ActionResult> AnalyzeAlert()
        {
            // v1.0.160.107 -- pin 3: identity FIRST, before the body read. HttpContext.Current does
            // not survive the first await, so a capture placed after ReadToEndAsync (as it was) can
            // silently see no user. CaptureLoginUser must precede AiDebugAllowed -- the latter reads
            // the fields the former populates.
            CaptureLoginUser();
            _roleSiteKeep = AiDebugAllowed();   // v1.0.160.108 H2: one role decision, pre-await
            string body;
            using (System.IO.StreamReader sr = new System.IO.StreamReader(Request.InputStream, Encoding.UTF8))
            {
                body = await sr.ReadToEndAsync().ConfigureAwait(false);
            }

            JObject ctx;
            try
            {
                ctx = JObject.Parse(body);
            }
            catch
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return Content("Bad JSON", "text/plain");
            }
            // v1.0.160.190: self-heal a thin context before analysis (same as the JSON path).
            if (_backfillCtxEnabled)
            {
                try { await BackfillContextAsync(ctx, default(System.Threading.CancellationToken)).ConfigureAwait(false); }
                catch (Exception bfx) { AiLog("WARN", "BACKFILL", "context backfill skipped: " + SanitizeJsonError(bfx.Message)); }
            }

            _traceActive = true; // timing always accumulates; file writes gated separately
                                 // v1.0.160.107: capture already done at the action entry (see top of AnalyzeAlert).
            _traceId = "sse-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N").Substring(0, 12);
            _reqStartUtc = DateTime.UtcNow;   // v1.0.160.57: for the audit totalMs
            _auditAnalysisId = 0;             // v1.0.160.73
            _trModelMs = 0; _trToolMs = 0; _trDiscoveryMs = 0; _trTurns = 0; _circuitSkipReason = null;
            _trAnalysisTurns = 0; _trToolCallMsSum = 0; _trPrefetchWallMs = 0; _trInLoopWallMs = 0; _trSlowestTool = null; _trSlowestToolMs = 0; _trDistinctTools = 0; lock (_trendLock) { _trTagFetches.Clear(); }
            _trBytesSent = 0; _trBytesRecv = 0; _trToolBytes = 0; _trToolBytesKept = 0;
            _trTokIn = 0; _trTokOut = 0; _trTokCacheRead = 0; _trTokCacheWrite = 0;
            _trToolCallCount = 0;
            JObject rs0 = new JObject();
            rs0["endpoint"] = "AnalyzeAlert"; rs0["alertId"] = GetCtx(ctx, "alertId");
            TraceAnalyze("request_start", rs0);

            _prefetchCtx = ctx;
            // v1.0.160.1: role gate merged from the other team's drop -- a non-site-keeping user is
            // forced onto QUANTUM (deepseek) server-side, so hiding the picker is presentation only.
            // v1.0.160.108 H2a: role captured ONCE before the body-read await (top of the action);
            // the late SafeIsSiteKeeping() call is gone -- after an await HttpContext.Current may be
            // null, so a late read can silently return false and mis-gate.
            bool _siteKeep = _roleSiteKeep;
            if (_siteKeep) { AiLog("INFO", "GATE", "site-keeping active for this request"); }
            _provider = GateProviderForRole(ResolveEngineAlias(GetCtx(ctx, "provider")), _siteKeep);   // v1.0.160.107: opaque id -> raw BEFORE gating
            _thinkReq = ParseThinkCtx(GetCtx(ctx, "think"));   // v1.0.160.42 UI toggle
                                                               // v1.0.160.73: open the audit row AFTER the provider/model are resolved, since the
                                                               // row records them. Returns 0 if the DB is off, dormant, or the route is absent --
                                                               // and 0 simply means no child writes happen. Nothing here can fail the verdict.
            _auditAnalysisId = AuditStartAnalysis(ctx);

            // v1.0.160.189: expose AnalysisId as a response header (also on the SSE path). Harmless if
            // headers are already flushed; wrapped.
            if (_auditAnalysisId > 0)
            {
                try
                {
                    Response.Headers["X-Analysis-Id"] = _auditAnalysisId.ToString();
                    Response.Headers["Access-Control-Expose-Headers"] = "X-Analysis-Id";
                }
                catch { }
            }

            // v1.0.160.188: link the analysis to its SOURCE row. The web reuses ctx.alertId for the id
            // in BOTH paths, so a discriminator decides the column: ctx.source == "pending" (or
            // ctx.isPending true, or an explicit ctx.pendingAlertApprovalId) => the id is a
            // PendingAlertApproval.Id; otherwise it is an FRSAlert.Id. Exactly one id column is set.
            // The [SQLLINK] log prints what the context carried so you can verify each path.
            if (_analysisLinkEnabled && _auditAnalysisId > 0)
            {
                long _idVal = 0; long.TryParse((GetCtx(ctx, "alertId") ?? "").Trim(), out _idVal);
                long _explicitPending = 0; long.TryParse((GetCtx(ctx, "pendingAlertApprovalId") ?? "").Trim(), out _explicitPending);
                string _src = (GetCtx(ctx, "source") ?? "").Trim().ToLowerInvariant();
                string _isPending = (GetCtx(ctx, "isPending") ?? "").Trim().ToLowerInvariant();
                bool _pending = _explicitPending > 0
                    || _src == "pending" || _src == "pendingalertapproval"
                    || _isPending == "true" || _isPending == "1";

                long _pendingId = _explicitPending > 0 ? _explicitPending : (_pending ? _idVal : 0);
                int _frsId = 0; if (!_pending && _idVal > 0 && _idVal <= int.MaxValue) { _frsId = (int)_idVal; }

                AiLog("INFO", "SQLLINK", "link source=" + (_pending ? "pending" : "frs")
                    + " id=" + _idVal + " (src='" + _src + "' isPending='" + _isPending + "' explicitPending=" + _explicitPending + ")"
                    + " analysisId=" + _auditAnalysisId);
                try
                {
                    if (_pendingId > 0) { WriteAnalysisLink(0, _pendingId, _auditAnalysisId); }
                    else if (_frsId > 0) { WriteAnalysisLink(_frsId, 0, _auditAnalysisId); }
                }
                catch (Exception lex) { AiLog("WARN", "SQLLINK", "FRSAlert_AIAnalysis upsert skipped: " + SanitizeJsonError(lex.Message)); }
            }

            // v1.0.160.79: reuse a stored analysis when it is still valid. Returns null on ANY doubt
            // -- DB off, dormant, miss, stale, unparseable -- and null simply means analyse normally.
            bool _reRun = string.Equals(GetCtx(ctx, "force"), "true", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            JObject _cachedEnv = TryServeFromCache(ctx, _reRun);
            if (_cachedEnv != null)
            {
                try
                {
                    // v1.0.160.147: UNWRAP. TryServeFromCache returns the stored ENVELOPE, which is
                    // {"verdict":{...}}. Wrapping it again produced {"verdict":{"verdict":{...}}},
                    // so the browser read every field one level too deep -- likely_cause, category,
                    // action and confidence all resolved to undefined, and served_from_cache sat on
                    // the inner object where the badge never looked. That is the INCONCLUSIVE / 0% /
                    // all-dashes render WITH a FRESH ANALYSIS badge on a run the log recorded as a
                    // cache HIT. The fresh path sends the verdict object itself, so the cached path
                    // must send the same shape, not a shape one level deeper.
                    // v1.0.160.180: a cached verdict may have been produced while the alert was
                    // ACTIVE, in which case its stored context_patch carries an empty resetTime and
                    // the panel would print "Still active" even after the alert has cleared. Re-check
                    // the LIVE FRS row and, only when it is now reset, inject the current stamp so the
                    // served panel shows the exact current state. Gated to the empty-reset case: a
                    // cache that already holds a reset is finished history that cannot change, so it
                    // keeps its zero-latency serve and adds no fetch.
                    try
                    {
                        JObject _cpChk = _cachedEnv["context_patch"] as JObject;
                        string _cachedRst = (_cpChk != null && _cpChk["resetTime"] != null) ? _cpChk["resetTime"].ToString() : "";
                        if (_cachedRst.Length == 0)
                        {
                            string _liveRst = await TryLiveResetTimeAsync(ctx, System.Threading.CancellationToken.None).ConfigureAwait(false);
                            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_liveRst))
                            {
                                if (_cpChk == null) { _cpChk = new JObject(); _cachedEnv["context_patch"] = _cpChk; }
                                _cpChk["resetTime"] = _liveRst;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    catch { }
                    // v1.0.160.149: replay the side blocks BEFORE the verdict, in the order a fresh
                    // run emits them -- the view merges context_patch before it renders, so sending
                    // it after the verdict would arrive too late to be used.
                    try
                    {
                        JObject _cp = _cachedEnv["context_patch"] as JObject;
                        if (_cp != null && _cp.Count > 0) { WriteSse("context_patch", new { patch = _cp }); }
                        JObject _ac = _cachedEnv["asset_condition"] as JObject;
                        if (_ac != null) { WriteSse("asset_condition", new { asset_condition = _ac }); }
                        JObject _sn = _cachedEnv["snapshot"] as JObject;
                        if (_sn != null) { WriteSse("snapshot", new { snapshot = _sn }); }
                    }
                    catch { }
                    JObject _cachedVerdict = (_cachedEnv["verdict"] as JObject) ?? _cachedEnv;
                    WriteSse("verdict", new { verdict = _cachedVerdict });
                    WriteSse("stats", new { cached = true });
                    // v1.0.160.138 (audit Gap 1): CLOSE the row this request opened. Without this,
                    // AuditStartAnalysis fires, the verdict is served from store, and the method
                    // returns leaving the row RUNNING forever -- which then blocks the cache for that
                    // alert on every later open. Serving from store is still an operator action worth
                    // recording, so it is completed with a servedFromCache marker rather than not
                    // opened at all.
                    try
                    {
                        // v1.0.160.140: carry the SERVED verdict into the row. Completing with an
                        // empty _lastResponseFull would write a COMPLETED row with no payload -- and
                        // a payload-less COMPLETED row is exactly what blocked this alert's cache in
                        // the first place. Closing an audit row must not manufacture the next
                        // blockage.
                        try
                        {
                            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_lastResponseFull) && _cachedEnv != null)
                            { _lastResponseFull = _cachedEnv.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None); }
                        }
                        catch { }
                        JObject _cAudit = new JObject();
                        _cAudit["servedFromCache"] = true;
                        AuditCompleteAnalysis(_cAudit, false, null);
                    }
                    catch { }
                }
                catch { }
                try { Response.Write("data: [DONE]\n\n"); Response.Flush(); } catch { }
                return new EmptyResult();
            }
            // Same per-request state the verdict path sets up. Without it the streaming
            // popup ran with NO argument clamps, NO budget caps, NO usability check and
            // NO payload narrowing -- every safeguard built for verdicts was skipped on
            // the path a user actually watches.
            _jsonToolUsed = new Dictionary<string, int>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            _jsonToolTotal = 0;
            _jsonToolOk = 0;
            _jsonAssetHints = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            _prefetchDone = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
            _jsonToolTrace = new List<string>();
            lock (_jsonDiagLock) { _jsonDiag = new List<string>(); }
            DateTime incSse;
            _incidenceEpoch = TryParseAlertTime(GetCtx(ctx, "time"), out incSse) ? ToEpochIst(incSse) : 0;
            string userMsg = BuildAnalyzeUserMessage(ctx);
            JObject pr0 = new JObject();
            pr0["promptVersion"] = "analyze-v1.0.9-narrative";
            pr0["system"] = TraceTrunc(RedactForTrace(AnalyzeSystemPrompt()), 20000);
            pr0["user"] = TraceTrunc(RedactForTrace(userMsg), 20000);
            // v1.0.160.68: reuse the SAME redacted+truncated text for the audit record, so the audit
            // inherits RedactForTrace rather than carrying a second, unredacted copy of the prompt.
            _lastPromptFull = pr0.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None);
            TraceAnalyze("prompt", pr0);
            JArray messages = new JArray();
            JObject um = new JObject();
            um["role"] = "user";
            um["content"] = userMsg;
            messages.Add(um);

            Response.ContentType = "text/event-stream";
            Response.Headers["Cache-Control"] = "no-cache";
            Response.Headers["X-Accel-Buffering"] = "no";
            Response.Buffer = false;
            Response.BufferOutput = false;

            // v1.0.55.11: emit the run traceId to the client (for the per-alert Tool trace lookup).
            // MUST be after the SSE headers above -- writing before them corrupts the stream.
            try { WriteSse("meta", new { traceId = _traceId }); } catch { }
            // v1.0.160.162: greeting header (option D), OFF by default, logged-in sessions only.
            // Emitted here so it paints before the first step. Never gates or delays the verdict.
            if (_greetingEnabled)
            {
                try
                {
                    string g = BuildGreeting(ctx, false);
                    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(g))
                    {
                        WriteSse("greeting", new { text = g });
                    }
                }
                catch { }
            }
            // v1.0.160.142: analysisId belongs HERE, with meta, for the same reason -- after the
            // headers. Emitting it at AuditStartAnalysis (v1.0.160.139) wrote to the stream before
            // the headers existed and blanked the popup.
            if (_auditAnalysisId > 0)
            { try { WriteSse("analysis_id", new { analysisId = _auditAnalysisId }); } catch { } }

            try
            {
                await RunAgenticLoop(messages, AnalyzeSystemPrompt(), true, true).ConfigureAwait(false);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                WriteSse("error", new { message = FriendlyError(ex) });
            }
            finally
            {
                JObject re0 = new JObject();
                re0["turns"] = _trTurns; re0["modelMs"] = _trModelMs;
                re0["toolMs"] = _trToolMs; re0["discoveryMs"] = _trDiscoveryMs;
                re0["tokIn"] = _trTokIn; re0["tokOut"] = _trTokOut;
                re0["cacheRead"] = _trTokCacheRead; re0["cacheWrite"] = _trTokCacheWrite;
                if (_lastVerdictSummary != null) { re0["verdict"] = _lastVerdictSummary; }
                re0["causeCode"] = GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode");   // v1.0.133.0: scope for candidate promote
                re0["siteId"] = GetCtx(ctx, "siteId");
                re0["station"] = GetCtx(ctx, "station");
                // v1.0.160.192: per-cause optimization trace -- surface the timing breakdown in the Log
                // section so you can see where an alert's response time went without the offline script.
                long _rqTotal = _trModelMs + _trToolMs + _trDiscoveryMs;
                re0["totalMs"] = _rqTotal;
                re0["prefetchWallMs"] = _trPrefetchWallMs;
                re0["inLoopWallMs"] = _trInLoopWallMs;
                re0["toolCallMsSum"] = System.Threading.Interlocked.Read(ref _trToolCallMsSum);
                re0["prefetchCalls"] = _trPrefetchCalls;
                re0["inLoopCalls"] = _trToolCallCount;
                re0["slowestTool"] = _trSlowestTool ?? "";
                re0["slowestToolMs"] = _trSlowestToolMs;
                re0["mode"] = _synthesisMode ? "synthesis" : "agentic";
                re0["coverage"] = _lastCoverageKind.ToString();
                try {
                    AiLog("INFO", "TIMING", "cause=" + GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode")
                        + " total=" + _rqTotal + "ms model=" + _trModelMs + " tool=" + _trToolMs
                        + " prefetch=" + _trPrefetchWallMs + " inLoop=" + _trInLoopWallMs
                        + " turns=" + _trTurns + " calls=" + (_trPrefetchCalls + _trToolCallCount)
                        + " slowest=" + (_trSlowestTool ?? "-") + ":" + _trSlowestToolMs + "ms"
                        + " mode=" + (_synthesisMode ? "synthesis" : "agentic"));
                } catch { }
                // v1.0.160.193: per-tag fetch breakdown for the Log -- each attr fetched with ms/bytes and
                // USED (in driver set / trigger) vs WASTED (fetched but not needed). Spot unwanted/heavy fetches.
                try
                {
                    string dset = (_driverSetStr ?? "").ToUpperInvariant();
                    JArray tagArr = new JArray();
                    List<JObject> snap; lock (_trendLock) { snap = new List<JObject>(_trTagFetches); }
                    long wastedMs = 0; int wastedN = 0;
                    foreach (JObject tf in snap)
                    {
                        string attr = tf["attr"] != null ? tf["attr"].ToString() : "";
                        bool used = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(attr) && dset.Contains(attr.ToUpperInvariant());
                        tf["used"] = used;
                        if (!used) { wastedMs += (long)(tf["ms"] ?? 0); wastedN++; }
                        tagArr.Add(tf);
                    }
                    re0["tagFetches"] = tagArr;
                    re0["tagFetchCount"] = snap.Count;
                    re0["tagWastedCount"] = wastedN;
                    re0["tagWastedMs"] = wastedMs;
                    if (wastedN > 0)
                    {
                        System.Text.StringBuilder wb = new System.Text.StringBuilder();
                        foreach (JObject tf in snap) { if (tf["used"] != null && !(bool)tf["used"]) { wb.Append(tf["attr"]).Append("(").Append(tf["ms"]).Append("ms) "); } }
                        AiLog("INFO", "TAGOPT", "cause=" + GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode") + " fetched=" + snap.Count
                            + " wasted=" + wastedN + " wastedMs=" + wastedMs + " -> " + wb.ToString().Trim());
                    }
                }
                catch { }
                TraceAnalyze("request_end", re0);
                // v1.0.160.57: the 7W audit record. try/catch so an audit failure can never affect a
                // verdict that has already been produced.
                if (_audit7W)
                {
                    try
                    {
                        JObject _a7 = Build7WAudit(ctx, "verdict", _reqStartUtc);
                        TraceAnalyze("audit_7w", _a7);
                        // v1.0.160.141: store the VERDICT before completing the row. Without this the
                        // SSE path writes AnalysisStatus=COMPLETED with AnalysisOutputJson empty, and
                        // the verdict cache can never serve it -- which is exactly what
                        // "stored row has no verdict payload" was reporting. The envelope is built the
                        // same way the JSON path builds it, so a served row and a fresh one match.
                        try
                        {
                            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_lastResponseFull) && _lastVerdictSummary != null)
                            {
                                JObject _env = new JObject();
                                _env["verdict"] = _lastVerdictSummary;
                                _lastResponseFull = _env.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None);
                            }
                        }
                        catch { }
                        AuditCompleteAnalysis(_a7, false, null);   // v1.0.160.73: same object as the JSONL
                        AuditRequestAndCalls(_a7, ctx);            // v1.0.160.78: Request + its MCP calls
                                                                   // v1.0.160.57: also push it to the client so the per-run Log download can carry
                                                                   // it. The "meta" event fires BEFORE the run (traceId only); the audit is only
                                                                   // known at the end, so it needs its own event. Emitted before [DONE].
                                                                   // v1.0.160.119: DO NOT SEND IT AT ALL unless privileged. The per-run
                                                                   // diagnostic is built client-side from this event, so withholding the event
                                                                   // is the actual control; redaction below is defence in depth, not the fix.
                                                                   // The server-side audit row and JSONL above are untouched -- ops keeps the
                                                                   // real values, which is where they belong.
                        if (_roleSiteKeep)
                        {
                            // v1.0.160.156: CALLING NAMES ONLY, even for privileged sessions (owner:
                            // "imprint calling names instead"). Always the redacted copy: engine
                            // keeps the opaque calling id, provider/model/providerUrl removed, and
                            // the serialised scrub catches vendor strings anywhere else. The team
                            // maps calling name -> vendor internally; the server-side audit row and
                            // JSONL keep the real values.
                            WriteSse("audit", new { audit = RedactAuditForClient(_a7, false) });
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            // Tell the client explicitly, so it can CLEAR any copy left over from an
                            // earlier privileged run in the same page.
                            WriteSse("audit_denied", new { reason = "restricted" });
                        }
                    }
                    catch { }
                }
                try { Response.Write("data: [DONE]\n\n"); Response.Flush(); } catch { }
            }

            return new EmptyResult();
        }

        // -- v1.0.6 rev2 -- service-to-service verdict endpoint. Returns ONE
        // JSON envelope; never streams. Auth: X-Internal-Api-Key vs appSettings
        // InternalApiKey. Cooperative cancellation: the loop observes the token
        // at every await/iteration boundary; the AI/MCP calls in flight at cancel
        // time (at most one model call or one parallel tool chunk of <=4) drain in
        // background -- observed, slot-counted and TTL-bounded (no abort available). Tool use is
        // ENFORCED read-only + budgeted in verdict mode (see JsonToolPermitted),
        // and the verdict is schema-validated + operational-action filtered.
        // No unhandled exception escapes this action (outer boundary below).
        [HttpPost]
        public async Task<ActionResult> AnalyzeAlertJson()
        {
            // v1.0.160.107 -- pin 3: identity FIRST, before Core reads the body.
            CaptureLoginUser();
            _roleSiteKeep = AiDebugAllowed();   // v1.0.160.108 H2
            try
            {
                return await AnalyzeAlertJsonCore().ConfigureAwait(false);
            }
            catch
            {
                // absolute outer boundary: manually built, serializer-free reply
                try { Response.StatusCode = 200; } catch { }
                return Content("{\"status\":\"model_error\",\"verdict\":null,\"meta\":{\"error\":\"internal\"}}", "application/json");
            }
        }

        // presetCtxJson != null  =>  IN-PROCESS call from another controller in
        // this application. The shared-key check and the HTTP body read are then
        // skipped: the caller is already inside the authenticated pipeline and
        // supplies the context directly. Everything after that -- budget,
        // grounding gate, schema validation, envelope -- is identical, so an
        // in-process verdict is byte-for-byte what the HTTP endpoint returns.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        // IN-PROCESS ENTRY POINT
        // Call this from another controller in the same application instead of
        // making the site issue an HTTP request to itself. No URL, no shared
        // key, no TLS, and no ASP.NET session-lock deadlock risk.
        //
        //   var ai = new AiChatController();
        //   ai.ControllerContext = this.ControllerContext;
        //   string envelopeJson = await ai.ProduceVerdictJsonAsync(ctxJson);
        //
        // Returns the SAME envelope JSON the HTTP endpoint returns. The caller's
        // own Response.StatusCode is preserved -- this never rewrites it.
        // ------------------------------------------------------------------
        public async Task<string> ProduceVerdictJsonAsync(string ctxJson)
        {
            int savedStatus = 200;
            try { savedStatus = Response.StatusCode; } catch { }
            try
            {
                ActionResult r = await AnalyzeAlertJsonCore(ctxJson ?? "").ConfigureAwait(false);
                ContentResult c = r as ContentResult;
                if (c != null && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(c.Content)) { return c.Content; }
                return "{\"status\":\"model_error\",\"verdict\":null,\"meta\":{\"error\":\"no content\"}}";
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                System.Diagnostics.Trace.TraceError("[ProduceVerdictJsonAsync] " + ex.ToString());
                return "{\"status\":\"model_error\",\"verdict\":null,\"meta\":{\"error\":\"internal\"}}";
            }
            finally
            {
                // the in-process path must not leak its status onto the caller
                try { Response.StatusCode = savedStatus; } catch { }
            }
        }

        private async Task<ActionResult> AnalyzeAlertJsonCore(string presetCtxJson = null)
        {
            DateTime t0 = DateTime.UtcNow;
            bool gateHeld = false;
            Func<string, object, ActionResult> envelope = (status, verdict) =>
            {
                JObject env = new JObject();
                env["status"] = status;
                env["verdict"] = verdict == null ? null : JToken.FromObject(verdict);
                JObject meta = new JObject();
                meta["promptVersion"] = "analyze-v1.0.9-narrative";
                meta["componentVersion"] = ComponentVersion;
                string cfgModel = UseOpenAi
                    ? ReadStr("OpenAiModel", "gpt-5.4")
                    : ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnthropicModel"];
                // v1.0.160.107 -- F1-response: the configured model id names the vendor. Masked for
                // EVERY browser response (privileged included); it remains in logs/audit.
                if (AiDebugAllowed()) { meta["model"] = "configured"; }
                meta["durationMs"] = (long)(DateTime.UtcNow - t0).TotalMilliseconds;
                meta["requestId"] = _jsonRequestId ?? "";
                if (_auditAnalysisId > 0)
                {
                    meta["analysisId"] = _auditAnalysisId;
                }
                meta["toolCalls"] = _jsonToolTotal;
                meta["toolSucceeded"] = _jsonToolOk;
                if (_evidenceProvenanceEnabled)
                {
                    // Item 6: surface the evidence-provenance tally on the verdict meta (best-effort).
                    // v1.0.160.182: ENFORCE first -- demote fabricated [fetched] claims when the alerting
                    // tag's history does not cover the incidence -- so the tally below reflects reality.
                    if (_provEnforceEnabled)
                    {
                        try { EnforceEvidenceProvenance(env["verdict"] as JObject, _lastCoverageKind); }
                        catch { }
                    }
                    try { JObject _prov = ComputeEvidenceProvenance(env["verdict"] as JObject); if (_prov != null) { meta["provenance"] = _prov; } }
                    catch { }
                }
                // v1.0.160.186 (#1/#4/#7): force viz.threshold (+metric/value/unit) from the card's
                // triggering condition so "The numbers" matches what fired -- lower rule -> max of the
                // FAIL thresholds (= max(avg*LD%, MinSafe)), higher rule -> min (= min(avg*LD%, MaxSafe)).
                if (_vizCardThresholdEnabled)
                {
                    try { OverrideVizThresholdFromCard(env["verdict"] as JObject, _prefetchCtx); }
                    catch { }
                }
                meta["bgReserved"] = System.Threading.Interlocked.CompareExchange(ref _jsonBgReserved, 0, 0);
                meta["turns"] = _trTurns;
                meta["modelMs"] = _trModelMs;
                meta["toolMs"] = _trToolMs;
                meta["discoveryMs"] = _trDiscoveryMs;
                meta["bytesSentToModel"] = _trBytesSent;
                meta["bytesRecvFromModel"] = _trBytesRecv;
                meta["toolBytesRaw"] = _trToolBytes;
                meta["toolBytesKept"] = _trToolBytesKept;
                if (_trTokIn > 0 || _trTokOut > 0)
                {
                    meta["tokensIn"] = _trTokIn;
                    meta["tokensOut"] = _trTokOut;
                    meta["promptCacheEnabled"] = _promptCache;
                    // enabled but never read => the marker is not reaching the API
                    // v1.0.160.110 SL6b: _trAnalysisTurns, NOT _trTurns. _trTurns includes the Hindi
                    // translation (a second billable call), so this fired on every bilingual
                    // single-turn run whether or not the cache was actually broken.
                    if (_promptCache && _trTokCacheRead == 0 && _trAnalysisTurns > 1)
                    {
                        // v1.0.160.108 H1: library name removed -- this string is server-side only now,
                        // but it must not name a vendor library even in the audit-facing object.
                        meta["promptCacheWarning"] = "cache enabled but 0 cache reads across "
                            + _trTurns + " turns -- the client may be dropping cache_control";
                    }
                    if (_trTokCacheRead > 0) { meta["tokensCacheRead"] = _trTokCacheRead; }
                    if (_trTokCacheWrite > 0) { meta["tokensCacheWrite"] = _trTokCacheWrite; }
                }
                if (status == "timeout") { meta["timingPartial"] = true; } // in-flight phases may not have recorded yet
                if (_jsonEvidenceArgs != null) { meta["evidenceArgs"] = _jsonEvidenceArgs; }
                if (_jsonFaultDetail != null) { meta["fault"] = _jsonFaultDetail; }
                meta["mode"] = _synthesisMode ? "synthesis (1 turn, no tools)" : "agentic";
                // v1.0.160.107 -- F1-response: opaque id only; the raw ProviderKind stays in the
                // audit row and the server log, never in a browser response.
                meta["provider"] = OpaqueProviderId(_provider != null ? _provider : ProviderKind);
                if (_prefetchGap != null) { meta["prefetchGap"] = _prefetchGap; }
                if (coverageDowngrade != null) { meta["coverageDowngrade"] = coverageDowngrade; }
                if (AlertingTagId() != null)
                {
                    meta["coverageTagId"] = AlertingTagId();
                    if (coverageTagPresumed) { meta["coverageTagPresumed"] = true; }
                }
                if (_aiCacheParamMissing) { meta["promptCacheWarning"] = "Domain.dll predates the cacheSystem parameter; caching is off"; }
                if (_jsonToolTrace != null && _jsonToolTrace.Count > 0)
                {
                    meta["toolTrace"] = string.Join(" | ", _jsonToolTrace);
                }
                string diag = SnapshotDiag();
                if (diag.Length > 0) { meta["diagnostics"] = diag; }
                if (_jsonCaptureError != null) { meta["error"] = SanitizeJsonError(_jsonCaptureError); }
                // v1.0.160.108 H1: emit a WHITELIST, built fresh. .107 masked only provider/model and
                // still shipped fault/toolTrace/diagnostics/promptCacheWarning/tokens/library-name to
                // every caller. A whitelist (not a filter over the existing object) means a key added
                // later is invisible by DEFAULT rather than leaking until someone notices.
                env["meta"] = PublicMeta(meta, _roleSiteKeep);
                // v1.0.160.112 SL12: its OWN field, not a caveat. Caveats hedge THIS verdict; a
                // standing condition is a separate finding with its own owner and action.
                JObject _assetCond = BuildAssetCondition();
                if (_assetCond != null) { env["asset_condition"] = _assetCond; }
                // v1.0.160.112 SL17: retrievedAt (NOT "asOf" -- analysis time is not measurement
                // time) plus the age from incidence, so a snapshot taken hours later cannot be read
                // as an at-alert reading. No occupancy claim: the TPR fetch ends at incidence+2h.
                if (_snapshotRetrievedAt != DateTime.MinValue)
                {
                    JObject snap = new JObject();
                    snap["retrievedAt"] = _snapshotRetrievedAt.ToString("dd/MM/yyyy HH:mm:ss");
                    DateTime _incF;
                    if (_prefetchCtx != null && TryParseAlertTime(GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "time"), out _incF))
                    { snap["ageFromIncidenceSec"] = (long)(_snapshotRetrievedAt - _incF).TotalSeconds; }
                    if (_snapshotValues != null && _snapshotValues.Count > 0) { snap["values"] = _snapshotValues; }
                    env["snapshot"] = snap;
                }
                // v1.0.160.110 SL7: return a MINIMAL patch the view merges into its stored context,
                // so the follow-up AnalyzeChat posts back populated fields. Mutating ctx server-side
                // does not reach the browser. Only these two keys -- never the full server context.
                if (_prefetchCtx != null)
                {
                    JObject patch = new JObject();
                    string stn = GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "station");
                    string atp = GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "assetType");
                    if (stn.Length > 0) { patch["station"] = stn; }
                    if (atp.Length > 0) { patch["assetType"] = atp; }
                    // v1.0.160.130: resetTime too. Same reason as assetType -- the browser cannot
                    // reliably derive it, and getting it wrong prints "Still active" on a cleared alert.
                    string rst = GetCtx(_prefetchCtx, "resetTime");
                    if (rst.Length > 0) { patch["resetTime"] = rst; }
                    if (patch.Count > 0) { env["context_patch"] = patch; }
                }
                JObject tv = new JObject();
                tv["status"] = status; tv["totalMs"] = meta["durationMs"]; tv["turns"] = _trTurns;
                tv["modelMs"] = _trModelMs; tv["toolMs"] = _trToolMs; tv["discoveryMs"] = _trDiscoveryMs;
                tv["toolCalls"] = _jsonToolTotal; tv["toolSucceeded"] = _jsonToolOk;
                tv["bytesSentToModel"] = _trBytesSent; tv["bytesRecvFromModel"] = _trBytesRecv;
                tv["toolBytesRaw"] = _trToolBytes; tv["toolBytesKept"] = _trToolBytesKept;
                tv["tokensIn"] = _trTokIn; tv["tokensOut"] = _trTokOut;
                tv["tokensCacheRead"] = _trTokCacheRead;
                // average sent per turn: the repetition cost of the agentic loop
                tv["avgSentPerTurn"] = _trTurns > 0 ? (_trBytesSent / _trTurns) : 0;
                // v1.0.160.98: `tv` is the TIMING envelope, not the verdict. Store the verdict
                // envelope instead, and only if the streaming path has not already captured one.
                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_lastResponseFull))
                {
                    try { _lastResponseFull = env.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None); } catch { }
                }
                // v1.0.160.186: close the row Item 1 opened. envelope() is the ONE choke point every
                // return path passes through, so a row cannot be left RUNNING. _prefetchCtx, not ctx:
                // this lambda is declared before ctx exists, so ctx is not in its scope. Early returns
                // (bad_request/unauthorized) never reach Start, so _auditAnalysisId is 0 and this is
                // skipped. try/catch: an audit failure must never affect a verdict already produced.
                if (_auditAnalysisId > 0)
                {
                    try
                    {
                        JObject auditRow = Build7WAudit(_prefetchCtx, "verdict-json", _reqStartUtc);
                        AuditCompleteAnalysis(auditRow, status != "ok", status == "ok" ? null : status);
                        AuditRequestAndCalls(auditRow, _prefetchCtx);
                    }
                    catch
                    {
                    }
                }
                TraceAnalyze("envelope", tv);
                AiLog(status == "ok" ? "INFO" : "WARN", "REQ",
                    "verdict end status=" + status + " turns=" + _trTurns
                    + " totalMs=" + meta["durationMs"] + " modelMs=" + _trModelMs + " toolMs=" + _trToolMs
                    + " tools=" + _jsonToolTotal + "/" + _jsonToolOk + "ok"
                    + " sent=" + _trBytesSent + "B recv=" + _trBytesRecv + "B"
                    + " tokIn=" + _trTokIn + " tokOut=" + _trTokOut
                    + (_jsonCaptureError != null ? " err=" + SanitizeJsonError(_jsonCaptureError) : ""));
                return Content(env.ToString(Formatting.None), "application/json");
            };
            try { Response.TrySkipIisCustomErrors = true; } catch { }

            if (presetCtxJson == null)
            {
                string cfgKey = ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["InternalApiKey"];
                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(cfgKey))
                {
                    Response.StatusCode = 403;
                    return envelope("disabled", null);
                }
                string gotKey = Request.Headers["X-Internal-Api-Key"];
                if (!FixedTimeEquals(cfgKey, gotKey))
                {
                    Response.StatusCode = 401;
                    return envelope("unauthorized", null);
                }
            }

            // read + validate BEFORE taking any permit, so slow/chunked bodies can
            // never occupy the gate; the read itself is byte-bounded AND time-bounded.
            string body;
            if (presetCtxJson != null)
            {
                if (presetCtxJson.Length > 262144)
                {
                    return envelope("bad_request", null);
                }
                body = presetCtxJson;
            }
            else
            {
                if (Request.ContentLength > 262144)
                {
                    Response.StatusCode = 400;
                    return envelope("bad_request", null);
                }
                System.Threading.CancellationToken earlyClientCt = System.Threading.CancellationToken.None;
                try { earlyClientCt = Response.ClientDisconnectedToken; } catch { }
                using (System.Threading.CancellationTokenSource readCts =
                    System.Threading.CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource(earlyClientCt))
                {
                    readCts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30));
                    try
                    {
                        body = await ReadBodyBoundedAsync(Request.InputStream, 262144, readCts.Token)
                            .ConfigureAwait(false);
                    }
                    catch
                    {
                        Response.StatusCode = 400;
                        return envelope("bad_request", null);
                    }
                }
            }
            if (body == null)
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return envelope("bad_request", null);
            }
            JObject ctx;
            try { ctx = JObject.Parse(body); }
            catch { Response.StatusCode = 400; return envelope("bad_request", null); }
            string shapeReason;
            if (!ValidateCtxShape(ctx, out shapeReason))
            {
                _jsonCaptureError = shapeReason;
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return envelope("bad_request", null);
            }
            if (GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode") == "" && GetCtx(ctx, "description") == "" && GetCtx(ctx, "alertId") == "")
            {
                Response.StatusCode = 400;
                return envelope("bad_request", null);
            }
            // v1.0.160.190: thin-context self-heal. When causeCode/siteId/assetId are missing but the
            // station+assetName+time are present, resolve them from the FRS alert record BEFORE analysis
            // (search_sites -> search_assets -> get_frs_alerts around time -> match this alert) so the
            // cause's dependent attributes + condition load from CauseToLogic/_gateById instead of the
            // model thrashing blind. Best-effort, gated, only fills blanks.
            if (_backfillCtxEnabled)
            {
                try { await BackfillContextAsync(ctx, default(System.Threading.CancellationToken)).ConfigureAwait(false); }
                catch (Exception bfx) { AiLog("WARN", "BACKFILL", "context backfill skipped: " + SanitizeJsonError(bfx.Message)); }
            }
            string callerReqId = Request.Headers["X-Request-Id"];
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(callerReqId)) { callerReqId = GetCtx(ctx, "requestId"); }
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(callerReqId) && callerReqId.Length > 128)
            {
                callerReqId = null; // oversized caller id: never echoed, fallback used
            }
            _jsonRequestId = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(callerReqId)
                ? callerReqId
                : GetCtx(ctx, "alertId") + "-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N").Substring(0, 12);
            _traceActive = true; // timing always accumulates; file writes gated separately
            _traceId = _jsonRequestId;
            _trModelMs = 0; _trToolMs = 0; _trDiscoveryMs = 0; _trTurns = 0; _circuitSkipReason = null;
            _trAnalysisTurns = 0; _trToolCallMsSum = 0; _trPrefetchWallMs = 0; _trInLoopWallMs = 0; _trSlowestTool = null; _trSlowestToolMs = 0; _trDistinctTools = 0; lock (_trendLock) { _trTagFetches.Clear(); }
            _trBytesSent = 0; _trBytesRecv = 0; _trToolBytes = 0; _trToolBytesKept = 0;
            _trTokIn = 0; _trTokOut = 0; _trTokCacheRead = 0; _trTokCacheWrite = 0;
            _trToolCallCount = 0;
            JObject rs = new JObject();
            rs["endpoint"] = "AnalyzeAlertJson"; rs["alertId"] = GetCtx(ctx, "alertId");
            AiLog("INFO", "REQ", "verdict start alert=" + GetCtx(ctx, "alertId")
                + " cause=" + GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode") + " asset=" + GetCtx(ctx, "assetName")
                + " station=" + GetCtx(ctx, "station")
                + " card=" + (ctx["alertCard"] != null ? "yes" : "NO"));
            TraceAnalyze("request_start", rs);

            DateTime incTime;
            _incidenceEpoch = TryParseAlertTime(GetCtx(ctx, "time"), out incTime) ? ToEpochIst(incTime) : 0;
            string userMsg = BuildAnalyzeUserMessage(ctx);
            if (userMsg.Length > 32000)
            {
                userMsg = userMsg.Substring(0, 32000) + " ...[context truncated]";
            }
            JObject pr = new JObject();
            pr["promptVersion"] = "analyze-v1.0.9-narrative";
            pr["system"] = TraceTrunc(RedactForTrace(AnalyzeSystemPrompt()), 20000);
            pr["user"] = TraceTrunc(RedactForTrace(userMsg), 20000);
            TraceAnalyze("prompt", pr);
            _prefetchCtx = ctx;
            _provider = ResolveEngineAlias(GetCtx(ctx, "provider"));   // v1.0.160.107: opaque id -> raw
            _thinkReq = ParseThinkCtx(GetCtx(ctx, "think"));   // v1.0.160.42 UI toggle
            // v1.0.160.186: open the audit row HERE too. Start must follow the provider/model
            // resolution (the row records them), and it must precede the loop so the id exists
            // when the envelope is built. Returns 0 when the DB is off/dormant/absent -- 0 simply
            // means no child writes and no analysisId, exactly as on the SSE path.
            _reqStartUtc = t0;
            _auditAnalysisId = AuditStartAnalysis(ctx);
            // v1.0.160.189: expose AnalysisId as a response header on AnalyzeAlertJson so the web can
            // read it off the response (reopen / rating / chat / SQL link) without parsing the body.
            if (_auditAnalysisId > 0)
            {
                try
                {
                    Response.Headers["X-Analysis-Id"] = _auditAnalysisId.ToString();
                    Response.Headers["Access-Control-Expose-Headers"] = "X-Analysis-Id";
                }
                catch { }
            }
            JArray messages = new JArray();
            JObject um = new JObject();
            um["role"] = "user";
            um["content"] = userMsg;
            messages.Add(um);

            int timeoutSec;
            if (!int.TryParse(ConfigurationManager.AppSettings["AnalyzeJsonTimeoutSec"], out timeoutSec) || timeoutSec <= 0)
            {
                timeoutSec = 120;
            }
            // v1.0.160.42 (owner rule): THINK runs 43-92s of hidden reasoning BEFORE any tool turn,
            // so the 120s deadline would kill a working run mid-verdict. With thinking on the
            // controller deadline is DISABLED. The request is still bounded by the DeepSeek
            // HttpClient timeout (DeepSeekHttpTimeoutSec, default 600) -- deliberately finite, since
            // AnalyzeMaxConcurrentVerdicts is 5 and a never-returning call would wedge a slot.
            if (UseDeepSeek && ThinkOn)
            {
                AiLog("INFO", "LIFE", "THINK on -- verdict deadline disabled (was " + timeoutSec + "s); bounded by DeepSeek HTTP timeout");
                timeoutSec = int.MaxValue / 1000;
            }

            // admission: RESERVE this request's worst-case abandonable weight
            // against the hard cap, then take a concurrency permit. Reservation
            // is settled by the wrapper-loop completion continuation below, so
            // there is no gap between gate release and background accounting.
            if (System.Threading.Interlocked.Add(ref _jsonBgReserved, _jsonMaxChunk) > _jsonBgOpCap)
            {
                System.Threading.Interlocked.Add(ref _jsonBgReserved, -_jsonMaxChunk);
                Response.StatusCode = 503;
                return envelope("busy", null);
            }
            bool reservationSettled = false;
            // v1.0.160.6: WAIT for a slot instead of instant-rejecting. WaitAsync (not .Wait)
            // keeps the request thread free while queued; the client-disconnect token abandons
            // the wait the moment the tab closes. Only a fully elapsed budget returns busy.
            // The reservation taken just above is HELD while queued -- deliberate, and why
            // _jsonBgOpCap is sized for running + queued.
            System.Threading.CancellationToken _admitCt = System.Threading.CancellationToken.None;
            try { _admitCt = Response.ClientDisconnectedToken; } catch { }
            bool _admitted = false;   // pre-initialised: rule 2 (CS0165) -- never rely on try/catch definite assignment
            try { _admitted = await _jsonGate.WaitAsync(_jsonAdmitWaitMs, _admitCt).ConfigureAwait(false); }
            catch (OperationCanceledException) { _admitted = false; }   // client left while queued
            catch (ObjectDisposedException) { _admitted = false; }      // token source torn down
            if (!_admitted)
            {
                System.Threading.Interlocked.Add(ref _jsonBgReserved, -_jsonMaxChunk);
                AiLog("WARN", "LIFE", "verdict admission timed out after " + _jsonAdmitWaitMs +
                    "ms (concurrency " + _jsonMaxConcurrent + ", queue " + _jsonQueueDepth + ")");
                Response.StatusCode = 503;
                return envelope("busy", null);
            }
            gateHeld = true;
            _jsonAbandonedW = 0;
            try
            {
                _jsonCapture = new StringBuilder();
                _jsonCaptureError = null;

                _jsonFaultDetail = null;
                lock (_jsonDiagLock) { _jsonDiag = new List<string>(); }
                _jsonToolUsed = new Dictionary<string, int>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
                _jsonToolTotal = 0;
                _jsonToolOk = 0;
                _jsonGotEvidence = false;
                _jsonGotHistory = false;
                gotUsableHistoryGet = false;
                requiredAlertingTagId = null;
                presumedAlertingTagId = null;
                coverageTagPresumed = false;
                coverageByTag = null;
                _derivedAlert = false;            // v1.0.82.0 rev J
                _derivedParam = null;
                _derivedInputs = null;            // v1.0.109.0
                _weatherCard = null;              // v1.0.119.0
                _trainContext = null;             // v1.0.160.33
                _computedVerdict = null;          // v1.0.160.37
                _gateDroppedLast = 0; _computedWonLast = false;   // v1.0.160.77
                _triageAlertsRaw = null; _triageAssetId = null; _triageCauseCode = null; _triageCurrentAlertId = null;  // v1.0.111.0
                _derivedComponentsAdequate = false;
                _cardHasFail = false; _isFailureAlert = false;   // v1.0.160.111 (BUG-5)
                _isTrackFailureCause = false;   // v1.0.160.170
                _rawHasBreach = false;   // v1.0.160.173
                _lastCoverageKind = CoverageStateKind.Unverifiable;
                coverageDowngrade = null;
                _jsonEvidenceArgs = null;
                _jsonToolTrace = new List<string>();
                _jsonAssetHints = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
                _prefetchDone = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

                System.Threading.CancellationToken clientCt = System.Threading.CancellationToken.None;
                try { clientCt = Response.ClientDisconnectedToken; } catch { }
                using (System.Threading.CancellationTokenSource linked =
                    System.Threading.CancellationTokenSource.CreateLinkedTokenSource(clientCt))
                {
                    Task loop = null;
                    try
                    {
                        loop = RunAgenticLoop(messages, AnalyzeSystemPrompt(), true, false, linked.Token);
                        // settles the reservation exactly once, AFTER any
                        // abandonment registration inside the loop has run:
                        // keep credits equal to the abandoned weight (those are
                        // released by the real tasks' own continuations),
                        // release the rest.
                        reservationSettled = true;
                        loop.ContinueWith(lt =>
                        {
                            var _ = lt.Exception; // observe
                            int kept = System.Threading.Interlocked.Exchange(ref _jsonAbandonedW, 0);
                            if (kept > _jsonMaxChunk) { kept = _jsonMaxChunk; }
                            System.Threading.Interlocked.Add(ref _jsonBgReserved, -(_jsonMaxChunk - kept));
                        });
                        Task deadline = Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(timeoutSec));
                        Task disconnect = Task.Delay(System.Threading.Timeout.Infinite, linked.Token);
                        Task done = await Task.WhenAny(loop, deadline, disconnect).ConfigureAwait(false);
                        if (done != loop)
                        {
                            // the UNDERLYING client call in flight is counted inside
                            // AwaitWithCancel; the wrapper loop needs observation only.
                            linked.Cancel();
                            ObserveAbandoned(loop);
                            AiLog("WARN", "LIFE", "deadline " + timeoutSec + "s reached after " + _trTurns + " turns");
                            return envelope("timeout", null);
                        }
                        await loop.ConfigureAwait(false);
                    }
                    catch (OperationCanceledException)
                    {
                        if (linked.Token.IsCancellationRequested)
                        {
                            if (loop != null) { ObserveAbandoned(loop); }
                            return envelope("timeout", null);
                        }
                        _jsonCaptureError = "AI request timed out";
                        return envelope("model_error", null);
                    }
                    catch (ClientBusyException)
                    {
                        if (loop != null && !loop.IsCompleted) { ObserveAbandoned(loop); }
                        _jsonCaptureError = "client busy";
                        AiLog("WARN", "LIFE", "client lock unavailable -- refusing rather than running unserialized");
                        Response.StatusCode = 503;
                        return envelope("busy", null);
                    }
                    catch (Exception ex)
                    {
                        if (loop != null && !loop.IsCompleted) { ObserveAbandoned(loop); }
                        AiLogEx("LIFE", "agentic loop threw", ex);
                        _jsonFaultDetail = DescribeFault(ex);
                        if (_jsonCaptureError == null) { _jsonCaptureError = FriendlyError(ex); }
                        return envelope("model_error", null);
                    }
                }

                if (_jsonCaptureError != null)
                {
                    return envelope("model_error", null);
                }
                string text = _jsonCapture.ToString().Trim();
                _jsonCapture = null;
                if (text.Length == 0)
                {
                    _jsonCaptureError = "no verdict text produced (empty response or step limit)";
                    AiLog("WARN", "VERDICT", "no text after " + _trTurns + " turns (step limit " + _maxIter + ")");
                    return envelope("model_error", null);
                }
                if (!_jsonGotEvidence || !_jsonGotHistory)
                {
                    // ok requires at least one USABLE history/trend result (value
                    // evidence), not merely a baseline or alert lookup.
                    _jsonCaptureError = "no usable history/baseline/alert evidence; verdict ungrounded";
                    AiLog("WARN", "GROUND", "gate failed: evidence=" + _jsonGotEvidence
                        + " history=" + _jsonGotHistory + " | " + SnapshotDiag());
                    return envelope("ungrounded", null);
                }
                if (text.IndexOf("```", StringComparison.Ordinal) >= 0)
                {
                    text = text.Replace("```json", "").Replace("```", "").Trim();
                }
                JObject verdictObj = null;
                try { verdictObj = JObject.Parse(text); }
                catch
                {
                    // The model sometimes wraps the object in a sentence ("Here is
                    // the verdict: {...}"). Salvage the outermost balanced object
                    // rather than discarding a good verdict over its packaging.
                    verdictObj = ExtractFirstJsonObject(text);
                }
                if (verdictObj == null)
                {
                    _jsonCaptureError = "verdict not valid JSON";
                    AiLog("WARN", "VERDICT", "model output was not JSON and could not be salvaged");
                    return envelope("model_error", null);
                }
                string schemaReason;
                if (!ValidateAndSanitizeVerdict(verdictObj, out schemaReason))
                {
                    _jsonCaptureError = "verdict schema invalid: " + schemaReason;
                    AiLog("WARN", "VERDICT", "schema rejected: " + schemaReason);
                    return envelope("model_error", null);
                }
                // v1.0.111.0: attach server-computed derived_inputs (raw values behind the derived
                // alert + which showed the LARGEST DEVIATION) for the card - structured numeric
                // data, independent of the model's text. SUPPRESSED when the verdict is
                // INCONCLUSIVE or component coverage is inadequate: a "we don't know" verdict must
                // not display an input-deviation panel that implies a settled cause.
                if (ShouldAttachDerivedInputs(verdictObj)) { verdictObj["derived_inputs"] = _derivedInputs; }
                // v1.0.111.0: attach server-VERIFIED triage (from parsed same-asset/same-cause
                // alert history), suppressed on INCONCLUSIVE / inadequate history.
                AttachTriageIfEligible(verdictObj);
                // v1.0.119.0: attach the card-shaped weather (server-only key) so the WEATHER tile
                // shows the real rain/thunderstorm data instead of "pending".
                if (_weatherCard != null) { verdictObj["weather"] = _weatherCard; }
                if (_trainContext != null) { verdictObj["train_context"] = _trainContext; }   // v1.0.160.33
                // v1.0.160.98: capture the VERDICT for AI_ALERT_Analysis.AnalysisOutputJson. It must
                // be taken HERE -- on the streaming path the UI actually uses, and at the point
                // verdictObj is fully built (sanitised, triage/weather/train attached) -- so a cache
                // hit renders exactly what the first operator saw.
                // Previously assigned in AnalyzeAlertJsonCore (the JSON BATCH path, never executed by
                // the UI) and from `tv`, the TIMING envelope -- so the column was empty, and would
                // have held stopwatch numbers rather than an analysis.
                try { _lastResponseFull = verdictObj.ToString(Newtonsoft.Json.Formatting.None); } catch { }
                // v1.0.108.0 / hardened 1.0.111.0: bilingual. verdictObj is FULLY SANITIZED
                // (operational-action filtered + length-trimmed). AttachHinglishAsync translates the
                // SANITIZED fields under the AI lock, with its own timeout+cancellation, and records
                // its tokens - so the Hindi INHERITS the safety and the "one call" accounting stays
                // honest. Best-effort: a translation failure leaves the English verdict untouched.
                if (_bilingualHindi)
                {
                    try { await AttachHinglishAsync(verdictObj, clientCt).ConfigureAwait(false); }
                    catch (Exception exTr) { AiLog("WARN", "HI", "hinglish translate failed (English verdict unaffected): " + SanitizeJsonError(exTr.Message)); }
                }
                // v1.0.160.7: assemble the notification "push" block from the (now fully
                // sanitized + optionally translated) verdict. Pure string composition, no model,
                // no lock. Best-effort: a failure must never sink a good verdict.
                try { verdictObj["push"] = BuildPushBlock(verdictObj, ctx); }
                catch (Exception exPush) { AiLog("WARN", "PUSH", "push block build failed (verdict unaffected): " + SanitizeJsonError(exPush.Message)); }
                return envelope("ok", verdictObj);
            }
            finally
            {
                if (gateHeld) { _jsonGate.Release(); }
                if (gateHeld && !reservationSettled)
                {
                    // loop never started: nothing could have been abandoned
                    System.Threading.Interlocked.Add(ref _jsonBgReserved, -_jsonMaxChunk);
                }
            }
        }

        // v1.0.160.7: notification payload builder. Everything here is READ from an
        // already-sanitized verdictObj (operational-action filtered, length-trimmed) plus the
        // request ctx; it writes only the "push" object. No model call, no I/O, no lock.
        private static string PushStr(JToken t) { return t == null || t.Type == JTokenType.Null ? "" : t.ToString().Trim(); }

        // word-safe truncation: never splits a number or a word; appends a single ellipsis.
        private static string PushTrunc(string s, int max)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) { return ""; }
            s = System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.Replace(s, "\\s+", " ").Trim();
            if (s.Length <= max) { return s; }
            int cut = s.LastIndexOf(' ', Math.Min(max - 1, s.Length - 1));
            if (cut < max * 0.6) { cut = max - 1; }   // one very long token: hard cut rather than lose most of the line
            return s.Substring(0, cut).TrimEnd(' ', ',', ';', '.', '-', ':') + "\u2026";
        }

        // a controller-decision decline is NOT an instruction: the push must not present it as one.
        private static bool PushIsDecline(string action)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(action)) { return true; }
            string a = action.ToLowerInvariant();
            return a.Contains("cannot make that determination")
                || a.Contains("belongs to the section controller")
                || a.Contains("operational decision");
        }

        private static string PushColour(string verdict)
        {
            string v = (verdict ?? "").ToUpperInvariant();
            if (v.Contains("CONFIRM")) { return "red"; }
            if (v.Contains("LIKELY")) { return "amber"; }
            if (v.Contains("INCONCLUSIVE") || v.Contains("UNVERIF")) { return "grey"; }
            if (v.Contains("FALSE") || v.Contains("TRANSIENT") || v.Contains("NO ")) { return "green"; }
            return "grey";
        }

        private static string PushFirstSentence(string s)
        {
            if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(s)) { return ""; }
            int i = s.IndexOfAny(new[] { '.', ';' });
            return (i > 0 ? s.Substring(0, i) : s).Trim();
        }

        // Build one {type1,type2} pair from a source field-set (English or Hinglish).
        private static JObject PushPair(string verdict, string confPct, string category,
            string headline, string likelyCause, string action, string caveats, string evi0, string evi1)
        {
            string vlabel = (verdict + " " + confPct).Trim();
            bool decline = PushIsDecline(action);

            string t1body = vlabel + (string.IsNullOrEmpty(headline) ? "" : " \u2014 " + headline)
                + (decline ? "" : (string.IsNullOrEmpty(action) ? "" : " \u2192 " + PushFirstSentence(action)));

            string t2header = vlabel
                + (string.IsNullOrEmpty(category) ? "" : " \u00b7 " + category)
                + (string.IsNullOrEmpty(likelyCause) ? "" : " \u2014 " + likelyCause);

            System.Text.StringBuilder foot = new System.Text.StringBuilder();
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(evi0)) { foot.Append(evi0); }
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(evi1)) { foot.Append(foot.Length > 0 ? " \u00b7 " : "").Append(evi1); }
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(action)) { foot.Append(decline ? (" " + action) : (" \u2192 " + action)); }
            if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(caveats)) { foot.Append(" Caveat: ").Append(caveats); }

            JObject o = new JObject();
            o["header"] = PushTrunc(t2header, 120);
            o["footer"] = PushTrunc(foot.ToString(), 480);
            o["body"] = PushTrunc(t1body, 180);
            return o;
        }

        private static JObject BuildPushBlock(JObject v, JObject ctx)
        {
            string asset = GetCtx(ctx, "assetName");
            string station = GetCtx(ctx, "station");
            string cause = GetCtx(ctx, "causeCode");
            string verdict = PushStr(v["verdict"]);
            string confPct = v["confidence"] != null && v["confidence"].Type != JTokenType.Null
                ? PushStr(v["confidence"]) + "%" : "";
            string category = PushStr(v["category"]);
            string headline = PushStr(v["headline"]);
            string likely = PushStr(v["likely_cause"]);
            string action = PushStr(v["recommended_action"]);
            string caveats = PushStr(v["caveats"]);
            JArray evi = v["evidence"] as JArray;
            string e0 = (evi != null && evi.Count > 0) ? PushStr(evi[0]) : "";
            string e1 = (evi != null && evi.Count > 1) ? PushStr(evi[1]) : "";

            string title = "AI review \u00b7 " + (asset + " " + station).Trim()
                + (string.IsNullOrEmpty(cause) ? "" : " \u00b7 " + cause);

            JObject en = PushPair(verdict, confPct, category, headline, likely, action, caveats, e0, e1);

            JObject push = new JObject();
            JObject type1 = new JObject();
            type1["title"] = PushTrunc(title, 65);
            type1["body"] = en["body"];
            push["type1"] = type1;
            JObject type2 = new JObject();
            type2["header"] = en["header"];
            type2["footer"] = en["footer"];
            push["type2"] = type2;

            // Hinglish twins from the hi{} block, if present. hi carries the English action as
            // recommended_action_en (action stays English by design), so the Hindi push reuses it.
            JObject hi = v["hi"] as JObject;
            if (hi != null)
            {
                string hHead = PushStr(hi["headline"]);
                string hLikely = PushStr(hi["likely_cause"]);
                string hCav = PushStr(hi["caveats"]);
                string hAction = PushStr(hi["recommended_action_en"]);
                if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(hAction)) { hAction = action; }
                JArray hEvi = hi["evidence"] as JArray;
                string he0 = (hEvi != null && hEvi.Count > 0) ? PushStr(hEvi[0]) : "";
                string he1 = (hEvi != null && hEvi.Count > 1) ? PushStr(hEvi[1]) : "";
                JObject hiPair = PushPair(verdict, confPct, category, hHead, hLikely, hAction, hCav, he0, he1);
                JObject t1h = new JObject();
                t1h["title"] = PushTrunc(title, 65);
                t1h["body"] = hiPair["body"];
                push["type1_hi"] = t1h;
                JObject t2h = new JObject();
                t2h["header"] = hiPair["header"];
                t2h["footer"] = hiPair["footer"];
                push["type2_hi"] = t2h;
            }

            JObject meta = new JObject();
            meta["verdict"] = verdict;
            if (v["confidence"] != null && v["confidence"].Type != JTokenType.Null) { meta["confidence"] = v["confidence"]; }
            meta["asset"] = asset;
            meta["station"] = station;
            meta["causeCode"] = cause;
            meta["category"] = category;
            meta["colour"] = PushColour(verdict);
            push["meta"] = meta;
            return push;
        }

        // ---- rev4 infrastructure ----
        // v1.0.160.6: concurrency is config-driven (was hard 2). These MUST stay above _jsonGate:
        // static field initializers run in textual order, so declaring them later would build the
        // semaphore from 0 and refuse every request.
        private static readonly int _jsonMaxConcurrent = ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeMaxConcurrentVerdicts", 5), 1, 16);
        // How many over-limit requests may QUEUE for a slot. A queued request holds its
        // reservation while waiting, so this also sizes the cap headroom below.
        private static readonly int _jsonQueueDepth = ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeJsonQueueDepth", 5), 0, 32);
        // How long a queued request waits before giving up with busy. 0 = old instant-reject.
        private static readonly int _jsonAdmitWaitMs = ClampCfg(ReadInt("AnalyzeJsonAdmitWaitMs", 25000), 0, 120000);
        private static readonly System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim _jsonGate =
            new System.Threading.SemaphoreSlim(_jsonMaxConcurrent, _jsonMaxConcurrent);   // max concurrent verdict requests
        // HARD background bound by RESERVATION: each admitted request reserves
        // MaxChunk credits up front (its worst-case in-flight abandonable work:
        // one model call OR one tool chunk). Credits are released only via the
        // wrapper-loop completion continuation -- which runs AFTER any
        // abandonment registration -- minus the weight of actually-abandoned
        // ops, each of which releases its own weight when the REAL client task
        // completes. Invariant: reserved >= live abandoned work at all times;
        // admission against the cap is therefore a true bound with no gap and
        // no double count. No TTL: never-completing ops keep refusing new work
        // (the fix is the client timeout, not forgetting live work).
        private const int _jsonMaxChunk = 4;
        private static int _jsonBgReserved;
        // v1.0.160.6: DERIVED from the concurrency setting so the two admission gates can never
        // disagree. Sized for running + queued: a waiter reserves its worst-case weight while it
        // is queued, so at exactly _jsonMaxConcurrent*_jsonMaxChunk the running requests consume
        // the whole cap and every waiter would be bounced by the reservation check BEFORE it
        // reached the wait -- making the queue useless. Still explicitly overridable.
        private static readonly int _jsonBgOpCap = ClampCfg(
            ReadInt("AnalyzeJsonBgOpCap", (_jsonMaxConcurrent + _jsonQueueDepth) * _jsonMaxChunk),
            _jsonMaxChunk, 512);
        private static readonly bool _jsonParallelTools = ReadBool("AnalyzeJsonParallelTools", false);
        private int _jsonAbandonedW; // this request's abandoned weight
